hadiths[605]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10891","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Every statement that resembles divorce, when its speaker intends divorce, it is divorce. If he intended one, it is one, and if he intended three, it is three, and if he did not intend anything, it is nothing."
"10892","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man said to his wife: Go, you are not lawful until you marry another husband. He said: He has made clear. I said: And divorce did not come out of his mouth? He said: It suffices him that he made clear; she has separated from him."
"10893","From Ibrahim, from Abd Allah ibn Ali ibn al-Saib, from Ibn Ujayr, from Rukanah ibn Abd Yazid, he said: I divorced my wife Suhaymah with al-battah, then I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that. So he made me swear three times what I intended, and I swore that I intended one, so he returned her to me for two remaining. Then he divorced her the second time in the era of Umar, then the third in the era of Uthman. And Ibn Jurayj mentioned the hadith of Abu Rukanah that he divorced her three."
"10894","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from one who heard Ibn Abbas, saying concerning a man who says to his wife: You are free from me, it is one."
"10895","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from al-Hasan, that he said: It is as three."
"10896","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a man who said to his wife: You are free, he said: If he intended divorce, it is divorce."
"10897","From Hushaym, from Mansur, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who says to his wife: You are chaste, he said: It is one."
"10898","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: When he says to his wife: Count, it is divorce."
"10899","From Mamar, from one who heard al-Hasan, saying: When he says: You are divorced, count, then if he intended two, it is two, otherwise it is one. Mamar said: Qatadah used to count it as two."
"10900","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who divorces his wife twice, then said: I have released you with kindness, he said: He is made to swear by Allah that he intended only the two divorces with which he divorced her. If he swears, he bears of that what he bears."
"10901","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a man who said to his wife: Count, count, count, it is three, unless he says: I was repeating the first, then it is upon what he said."
"10902","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: When he says: Count, it is one."
"10903","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, he said: I asked al-Shabi about the saying of a man: Count, while he intends three, he said: It is one."
"10904","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: If he divorces her once while intending three, it is one."
"10905","From al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-Hasan, he said: If he divorces her once while he intended three, it is one."
"10906","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ali said: Concerning his saying: You are divorced with the divorce of al-haraj, it is three; she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband. Mamar said: And al-Hasan used to say it."
"10907","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: At one time he used to say: It is three, and at another time he said: It is what he intended."
"10908","From Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abu al-Husayn, from Nuaym ibn Dujajah, he said: A sister of mine was under a man, and he divorced her once, then said to her: You are upon me haraj. He wrote concerning her to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said: She has separated from him, while he regards it as lighter upon him than his sandal."
"10909","From Husayn ibn Mihran, he said: al-Amash informed me, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, and from Nuaym ibn Dujajah, that he divorced his wife twice, then said to her: You are haraj. He asked Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said: It is not the lightest of them upon me."
"10910","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When a man says to his wife: Go and marry, it is one. Mamar said: And it reached me from him, from al-Hasan, that they both said: One, and he has more right to her."
"10911","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: When he says to his wife: Go and marry, it is nothing unless he intended divorce, then it is one, and he has more right to her."
"10912","From Mamar, from Tawus, from his father, he said: If a man said to his wife: Stand, go, and the like, while intending divorce, it is divorce."
"10913","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he said to a man who said to his wife: Marry, he said: If you intended divorce, it is divorce."
"10914","From al-Thawri, concerning his saying: Go, join, go out, and the like, he said: His intention. If he intended divorce, it is three, and if he intended one, it is one irrevocable, and if he did not intend anything, it is nothing, and it cannot be two."
"10915","From Mamar, from one who heard al-Hasan, saying concerning his saying: Join your family, he said: Intention."
"10916","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: I do not know it as divorce."
"10917","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a man who said to his wife: Go, for you are not lawful to me until you marry another husband, he said: He has made clear; it suffices him. She has separated from him."
"10918","From al-Thawri, from one who heard Ibrahim, saying concerning the saying of a man: You are not to me a wife, he said: It is a lie, unless he intended divorce."
"10919","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, he said: It is a lie, like the saying of Ibrahim about it."
"10920","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When he says: You are not to me a wife, it is one, if by that he intended divorce. Qatadah said: And I asked Ibn al-Musayyib about it, and he said: What did you hear about it? I said: It reached me that Yusuf ibn al-Hakam counted it as one, and he said: How far. He said: As for a man who said to his wife: You are not to me a wife, you do not obey my command, while he does not intend divorce, it is nothing."
"10921","From Abd Allah ibn Kathir, from Shubah, he said: And Hammad, I asked al-Hakam about a man who says: You are not to me a wife. Al-Hakam said: If he intended divorce, it is one irrevocable. And Hammad said: If he intended divorce, it is one, and he has more right to her."
"10922","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man said to his wife: Nothing of your affair is to me? He said: Bind him by oath. He said: I said: I have sent you away, you are not to me a wife, and the like. He said: Bind him. He said: As for what is clear to you, carry it upon it, and as for what is not upon you, bind him by it."
"10923","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Shubrumah, from al-Shabi, he said: He has no intention in what is apparent; intention is only in what is hidden from us."
"10924","From al-Thawri, concerning a man to whom it was said: Did you marry? He said: No. Ibrahim and al-Shabi said: It is a lie."
"10925","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: It is a lie."
"10926","From Mamar, from al-Hasan, he said: It is a lie."
"10927","From al-Thawri, concerning a man to whom it was said: Did you divorce your wife last year? He said: Yes. He said: As for in judgment, it binds him, and as for between him and Allah, it is a lie. This is what we take. He said: And Said ibn Jubayr was asked about it, and he said: It is a lie."
"10928","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, he said: Divorce binds him."
"10929","From Mamar, from Layth, from Mujahid, that a man said to his wife in the time of Umar: Your rope is upon your withers, your rope is upon your withers, your rope is upon your withers. Umar made him swear between the Corner and the Maqam, and he said: I intended divorce three times, so he carried it out upon him."
"10930","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Sulayman, that Umar ordered Ali to make him swear what he intended."
"10931","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When he says: Your rope is upon your withers, it is one, and what he intended, and he has more right to her."
"10932","From al-Thawri, from Mutarrif, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said concerning al-mawhubah: If they accept her, it is one, and if they do not accept her, it is nothing. From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from Ibrahim, like the saying of Ali."
"10933","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ali said: If they accept her, it is one, and if they do not accept her, it is nothing. From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from Ibrahim, like the saying of Ali."
"10934","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ali said: If they accept her, it is one irrevocable, and if they return her, it is one, and if they do not accept her, it is nothing."
"10935","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, the like, he said: It is one irrevocable."
"10936","From al-Thawri, from Ashath, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abd Allah, he said: Whether they accept her or do not accept her, it is nothing."
"10937","From Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abd Allah, he said: If they accept her, it is one irrevocable."
"10938","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that Zayd ibn Thabit said: If they accept her, it is three; she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband. And if they return her, it is one, and he has more right to her."
"10939","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: If they accept her, it is one, and he has more possession, and if they return her, it is nothing."
"10940","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabiah, he said: Any man who gifts his wife to her family and they divorce her three times, she has become free from him."
"10941","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ata, the like, he said: It is one irrevocable."
"10942","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When he says: I have freed your way, and I have no way over you, it is one and what he intended."
"10943","From Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Malik ibn Dinar, he said: I asked Ikrimah about a man who says to his wife: Join your family, while intending divorce, he said: One, and he has more right to her."
"10944","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: When a man has four wives, and said: Divide among you one divorce, or two, or three, or four, he has divorced each one of them one divorce each, until he says: Five or six or seven or eight, then whichever of that he said, he divorces them two divorces each, until he says: Divide among you nine, or above that, then when he says that, he divorces all of them."
"10945","From al-Thawri, from Abu Sahl, from al-Shabi, he said: When a man divorces part of a divorce, he said: There are no fractions in it; it is a complete divorce. And Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said it."
"10946","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: If he says: You are divorced a third of a divorce, or a quarter of a divorce, or a fifth of a divorce, or a sixth of a divorce, it is one."
"10947","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When he says: Your finger is divorced, she is divorced; divorce has fallen upon her."
"10948","From al-Thawri, he said: When he says: Your finger, or your hair, or anything of you is divorced, it is one divorce."
"10949","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: Concerning a man who said to his wife: You are divorced a houseful, he said: Qatadah separated between them."
"10950","From al-Thawri, he said: It is one, or what he intended."
"10951","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata was asked about a man who divorced once in the presence of one man, and once in the presence of another man, he said: They are nothing; each man witnessed only one."
"10952","From al-Thawri, from al-Shabi, he used to say: Concerning a man who divorces in the presence of two men, and one testifies to one divorce, and the other testifies to two divorces, he regarded it as disagreement."
"10953","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Shurayh, he said: If a man testified to a thousand dirhams, and a man to five hundred, the lesser is taken."
"10954","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When a man testifies to one divorce, and another to three, it is one, and the man is made to swear."
"10955","From al-Thawri, Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I asked al-Shabi and Abd Allah ibn Maqil about a man who divorced his wife, then a man met him and said: Did you divorce? He said: Yes. Then another met him and said: Did you divorce your wife? He said: Yes. Then another met him and said: Did you divorce your wife? He said: Yes. They said: His intention in that."
"10956","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Said, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that a man divorced his wife, then a man met him and said: Did you divorce your wife? He said: Yes. Then another met him and he said: Yes. Then another met him and he said: Yes. Then another met him and he said: Yes. That was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said: That is upon it, or that is what he intended."
"10957","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from a man who said to his wife: You are divorced one as a thousand, and he said: She is not lawful to him until she marries another husband. Sufyan said: As for our companions, they do not say that. They say: It is one, and he has more right to her."
"10958","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata was asked about two men who divorced or freed concerning a matter in which they differ, and no proof was established, he said: They are bound by oath."
"10959","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning two men who swear by divorce and by emancipation over a matter in which they differ, and no proof was established for either of them for his saying, he said: They are bound by oath, and they bear of that what they bear. From Mamar, he said: And one who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying like the saying of al-Zuhri."
"10960","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a man who has a claim upon a man, and the defendant said: I have paid, otherwise his wife is divorced. The claimant said: His wife is divorced if you paid me. He said: Upon the defendant is proof that he paid him. If he establishes proof, the wife of the claimant is divorced, and if he does not bring proof, the claimant swears by Allah that he did not pay me, then the wife of the defendant is divorced."
"10961","From al-Thawri, he said: They are bound by oath, and the wife of neither of them is divorced, and by it we take."
"10962","From al-Thawri, concerning two men who swear over a bird by divorce, that it is such, and the other says: It is such, he said: That is to them; they are bound by oath."
"10963","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by the divorce of his wife if the judge spoke concerning a man, then he waited a while, then was asked, and said: I spoke to him, and the judge denied, he said: He is bound by oath."
"10964","From Mamar, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who said to his wife: You are divorced if I have not given you such and such, and he has no proof of that, he said: The man is made to swear that he is truthful, and his wife is returned to him. Mamar said: And Qatadah said: The wife is made to swear that he is lying, then she is divorced."
"10965","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When a man and his wife differ, and the man says: I intended such, and she says: Rather it is such, the man is made to swear."
"10966","From Mamar, he said: And he was asked about a woman who swore by freeing her slaves that she would never marry, then she wanted marriage after, and al-Hasan and Qatadah said: They say: She sells them, then marries. He said: And the like of that reached me, from al-Qasim and Salim and Ubayd Allah ibn Umar. He said: al-Qasim and Salim were asked about her, and said: She sells them and marries. Mamar said: And I asked Ibn Shubrumah and others among the scholars of Kufah, and they said: If she sells them then marries, they are freed from her, and she returns the price."
"10967","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and Ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man who says: His wife is divorced, and his slave is free, if he does not do such and such, putting divorce and emancipation first, they said: When he does what he said, there is upon him neither divorce nor emancipation. They say: When he fulfills. From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, the like."
"10968","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, like the saying of Said and al-Hasan. I said to him: Some people say: It is a divorce when he begins with divorce. He said: No, rather he has more right to his condition."
"10969","From al-Thawri, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zubaydi, that he asked Said ibn Jubayr about a man who began with divorce, and said: You are divorced if you do such and such, then he fulfilled, he said: It is nothing. And by it Sufyan takes."
"10970","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, that he used to say: When he begins with divorce, it falls upon him, even if he fulfills."
"10971","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who married a woman, and she said to him: Do you have a wife? He said: Every wife is divorced three times except you. Ibrahim gave him verdict by the saying of Shurayh: He made divorce binding upon him when he began with it."
"10972","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man says to his wife: You are divorced if I do such and such, and if he strikes for it a named term, he said: He does not do it, even if he touches her."
"10973","From Hushaym, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who swore not to eat milk, then ate butter, he said: He has broken oath, because butter is from milk. If he swore not to eat butter, then ate milk, he has not broken oath. If he swore not to eat meat, then ate fat, he broke oath. If he swore not to eat fat, then ate meat, he has not broken oath."
"10974","From Mamar, concerning a man who swears to a man by divorce that he will pay him his right by such and such for a term he named, unless you delay me, then he delays him, and he says: I am upon an oath, he said: As for Ibn Shubrumah, he said: He has left his oath unless he renews an oath. As for me, I say he is upon his oath as he said."
"10975","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by divorce not to eat meat, then ate fish, he said: As for judgment, it falls upon him, and intention is between him and Allah."
"10976","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, that he entered upon a son-in-law of his, and there was something concerning meat from him, so he brought him fish, and he said: This is meat."
"10977","From al-Thawri, concerning a woman whose husband swore that she not speak to so-and-so by her divorce, then she met her, and his wife said: Who is this? She said: I am so-and-so. He said: She has spoken to her."
"10978","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore to his wife that he would not drink milk belonging to a people, then some was made from it, he said: Divorce falls upon her. He said: And if he swore not to eat food belonging to them, then drank milk and sawiq, he said: And he said: Milk is not food, and food is sawiq."
"10979","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by the divorce of his wife that none but you wear this garment, then he gave it to the tailor and it was stolen, and he said: Nothing is upon him unless he knows that it was worn."
"10980","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by the divorce of his wife that he would not speak to her for a month, then sent her a messenger to do such and such, he said: It is not speech."
"10981","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by the divorce of his wife that he would not speak to her for a month, then sent her a messenger to do such and such in a month or two months, then it seemed to him to do it in a month, he said: He does it if he wishes."
"10982","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by the divorce of his wife that he would not take her out of Sanaa, then sent to her from Makkah, and she came to him, he said: If he intended that he himself take her out, no divorce falls upon her, and if he intended that he take her out thus, and did not intend himself, then his messengers are like himself."
"10983","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by the divorce of his wife that she not enter the house of so-and-so, then she was carried until made to enter the house, he said: It is not divorce."
"10984","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by the divorce of his wife that he dispute with his sister, then she sent her husband and he disputed him, he said: He has broken oath when one of them dies that."
"10985","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by the divorce of his wife that he would not eat the food of so-and-so, then some of it was bought for him, or that other man gifted it to him, and the swearer ate of it, he said: Nothing is upon him, because it has left him, unless he specifies food itself."
"10986","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore to a man by the divorce of his wife that he would pay him his right on the day of the crescent, then if he pays him before that he breaks oath. I mentioned it to Mamar, and he said: What he said does not please me. If he intended to pay him between him and the crescent, he has not broken oath."
"10987","From Mamar, from Hammad, concerning a man with four wives, who swore by the divorce of one of them, and did not name, nor intend which of them, he said: He places his hand upon whichever of them he wishes. He said: And Amr informed me, from al-Hasan, the like."
"10988","From Mamar, he said: And Qatadah said: He divorces all of them. From Mamar, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, the like."
"10989","From Mamar, he said: Qatadah was asked about a man with four wives, one of them stole, and she was divorced three times, and all denied that they stole, and he knew it was one of them, and does not know which, he said: He is compelled to divorce each one of them once, until marriage becomes lawful for them."
"10990","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I heard him saying: If a man swears over his wife that she not go out, then another wife goes out, and it is said to him: This is your wife, and he thinks it is the other, and divorces her three times, he said: It is nothing. He said: And Ibn Tawus said the like of that, and said: Upon neither of them is divorce."
"10991","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi and al-Hakam, concerning a man who swears over a thing and there comes upon his tongue other than what he intends, al-Shabi said: His intention, and al-Hakam said: He is taken by what he spoke."
"10992","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: His intention."
"10993","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a man who swore by divorce, or an oath other than divorce, over a matter, and the matter is other than what he divorced over and swore, while he thought when he divorced or swore that it was so, he said: I see nothing upon him. Ibn Jurayj said: And Abd al-Karim said to me: The companions of Ibn Masud impose that upon him."
"10994","From al-Thawri, concerning a man with two wives who divorces one of them, while he thinks she is the other, he said: He is taken by the one he pointed to, and as for between him and Allah, his intention which he intended is taken."
"10995","From Hushaym, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man with two wives who forbade one of them from going out, then the one not forbidden went out, and he thought she was the one he forbade, and when he saw her, he said: So-and-so, did you go out? You are divorced. Ibrahim said: Both are divorced together. Hushaym said: And Yunus informed me, from al-Hasan, that he said: The one he intended is divorced."
"10996","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who said to his wife: If you go out, I shall divorce you, and he has two wives, and his other wife heard of that, and borrowed the clothes of the one threatened with divorce and wore them, then went out, and he saw her and divorced her thinking she was the one he forbade from going out, and he said: The one he intended is divorced. Mamar said: Some scholars said: Both are divorced together."
"10997","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore by the divorce of his wife that he would not speak to so-and-so for a month, then said after that: Unless it seems to me, he said: If the speech was continuous, he has exception, and if he cut it and fell silent then excepted after that, he has no exception."
"10998","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Misar, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah, I shall raid Quraysh. Then he fell silent, then said: If Allah wills."
"10999","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore to a man by the divorce of his wife that he would pay him his right by the term of its time, then the one sworn to said: Unless I grant you delay, and the swearer fell silent, he said: His exception is nothing, unless the swearer excepts."
"11000","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata was asked about a man who said to his wife: You are divorced when you give birth, may he touch her in between? He said: Yes, and she is not divorced until the term comes."
"11001","From al-Thawri, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, concerning a man who says: His wife is divorced if he does not do such and such, then one of them dies before he does, he said: They inherit from each other. Sufyan said: Breaking oath occurred only after death."
"11002","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Concerning a man who says to his wife: You are divorced if I do not marry over you, he said: If he does not marry over her until he dies or she dies, they inherit from each other. He said: And more beloved to me is that he fulfill his oath before that."
"11003","From Mamar, from Matar al-Warraq, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man who divorced if he does not do such and such, he said: He does not approach his wife until he does what he said. If he dies before he does, there is no inheritance between them."
"11004","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he used to say: He may tread her. If he dies and did not do, there is no inheritance between them."
"11005","From Mamar, from Qatadah, and he said: I heard Qatadah saying: If her waiting period passes before he does what he said, she has separated from him."
"11006","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said to him: That he tread her until the first of them dies."
"11007","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: When he says: You are divorced when such and such happens, a matter he does not know whether it will be or not, it is not divorce until that happens, and he may tread her in between, and if he dies before what he fixed, they inherit from each other."
"11008","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When a man says to his wife: You are divorced after a year, she is divorced the hour he says that. Qatadah mentioned it, from al-Hasan and Ibn al-Musayyib."
"11009","From Mamar, from Dawud, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: When he says: You are divorced after a year, she is divorced when he says that. Mamar said: And I heard al-Zuhri also saying that."
"11010","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: It is not divorce until the term comes, and they inherit from each other in between. From al-Nakhai and al-Shabi, the like of that."
"11011","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Said, from Ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man who divorces his wife for a term, he said: Divorce falls upon her then. Al-Thawri said: As for our companions, from Ibrahim, they said: It does not fall upon her until the term comes. And by it Sufyan takes. And Mamar said the like of that, from al-Nakhai and al-Shabi."
"11012","From al-Thawri, he said: Concerning a man who said to his wife: When you menstruate a menstruation, you are divorced, or said: Whenever you menstruate, you are divorced, he said: As for the one to whom he said: When you menstruate, you are divorced, then when she enters into blood, she is divorced. As for the one to whom he said: Whenever you menstruate a menstruation, then until she bathes from the end of her menstruation, because he does not take her back until she bathes."
"11013","From Hushaym, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh: That a case was disputed to him concerning a man who divorced his wife if he commits an offense in Islam, then he hired a mule to the bath of Ayan, then went beyond with it to Isbahan, sold the mule, bought wine with it and drank it. Shurayh said: If you wish, testify that he divorced her. He said: They kept repeating the story to him, and he repeated to them, and he did not regard it as an offense."
"11014","From al-Thawri, from Abu Hafs, he said: I heard Tawus saying: Al-zaman is two months or three until he fixes a time."
"11015","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Al-zaman is two years, and al-hin is six months."
"11016","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman al-Isbahani, he said: Ikrimah said: Al-hin is six months. Ibn al-Musayyib said: Ikrimah has uncovered it."
"11017","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who said to his wife: You are divorced if Allah the Exalted wills, he said: Tawus and Hammad said: Divorce does not fall upon her."
"11018","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man swears and says: If he does not do such and such, his wife is divorced, if Allah wills, and he breaks oath, his wife is not divorced when he excepted. And by it Abu Hanifah used to take, and the people upon it, and by it Abd al-Razzaq takes."
"11019","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: Divorce does not fall upon her."
"11020","From al-Thawri, from Ismail, from al-Hasan, he said: His exception is nothing."
"11021","From Mamar, from Qatada, he said: Divorce does not fall upon her, and Allah has willed divorce when He fixed its term."
"11022","From Ismail ibn Ayyash, he said: Humayd ibn Malik informed me that he heard Makhul narrating from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Muadh, Allah has not created on the back of the earth anything dearer to Him than emancipation, and Allah has not created on the face of the earth anything more hateful to Him than divorce. So when a man says to his slave: you are free if Allah wills, he is free and he has no exception, and when he says to his wife: you are divorced if Allah wills, he has his exception and there is no divorce upon him."
"11023","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If he says: you are divorced if Allah wills, then if he takes her back there is no breach of oath."
"11024","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father: Whoever swears and says: if Allah wills, he has his reservation so long as he has not risen from his sitting place."
"11025","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: One of the sons of Abu Rafi narrated to me, from Ikrima the freedman of Ibn Abbas, that Ibn Abbas said: Abd Yazid, the father of Rukana, and his brothers divorced Umm Rukana, and he married a woman from Muzayna. She came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: He avails me no more than this hair avails, for a hair she took from her head, so separate me from him. Zeal seized the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he summoned Rukana and his brothers, and said to those sitting with him: Do you see so-and-so resembling Abd Yazid in such-and-such, and so-and-so resembling him in such-and-such. They said: Yes. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Abd Yazid: Divorce her, so he did. Then he said: Take back your wife Umm Rukana. He said: I divorced her thrice, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I knew, take her back, and he recited the verse of al-Nisa. Ibn Jurayj said: And one of the sons of Hantab narrated to me that one of the Rukaniyyat was called al-Muzaniyya Suhayma bint Uwaymir."
"11026","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: One of the sons of Abu Rafi informed me, from Ikrima, that Ibn Abbas said: A man in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divorced his wife thrice, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said that he should take her back. He said: I have divorced her thrice. He said: I knew, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: O Prophet, when you divorce women then divorce them for their waiting period. He said: So he took her back."
"11027","From Mamar, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Divorce in the time of the Messenger of Allah and Abu Bakr and years of Umars caliphate, the divorce of three was one. Then Umar said: The people have hastened a matter in which they had deliberation, so if only we enforce it upon them. So he enforced it upon them."
"11028","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that Abu al-Sahba said to Ibn Abbas: Do you know that the three were made one in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr, and three years of Umars rule. Then Ibn Abbas said: Yes."
"11029","From Umar ibn Hawshab, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Tawus informed him, he said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas and with him was his freedman Abu al-Sahba, and Abu al-Sahba asked him about a man who divorces his wife thrice all together. Ibn Abbas said: They used to make it one in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr, and the reign of Umar except the least of it, until Umar addressed the people and said: You have become excessive in this divorce, so whoever says anything it shall be upon him as he uttered it."
"11030","Yahya ibn al-Ala informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid al-Ijli, from Ibrahim, from Dawud ibn Ubada ibn al-Samit, he said: My grandfather divorced a wife of his a thousand divorces, so my father went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Did your grandfather not fear Allah. As for three, they are his, and as for nine hundred and ninety-seven, they are transgression and wrongdoing. If Allah the Exalted wills He will punish him, and if He wills He will forgive him."
"11031","From al-Thawri, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, he said: Zayd ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: A man met a jesting man in Madina and said: Did you divorce your wife. He said: Yes. He said: How many. He said: A thousand. He said: So he was brought before Umar. He said: Did you divorce your wife. He said: I was only jesting. So he struck him with the stick and said: Three of that suffice you."
"11032","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, he said: A man came to Ali and said: I divorced my wife as many as the arfaj shrubs. He said: Take three from the arfaj and leave the rest. Ibrahim said: And Abu al-Huwayrith informed me, from Uthman ibn Affan, the like of that."
"11033","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Alqama ibn Qays, he said: A man came to Ibn Masud and said: I divorced my wife as many as the stars. Ibn Masud said something about the women of the people of the earth which I do not remember. He said: And another man came to him and said: I divorced my wife eight times. Ibn Masud said: Do these people want her to become separated from you. He said: Yes. Ibn Masud said: O people, Allah has made divorce clear, so whoever divorces as Allah commanded him has made it clear, and whoever confuses we hold his confusion against him. By Allah, do not confuse matters upon yourselves and then expect us to bear it for you. Yes, it is as he says. He said: And we think the saying of Ibn Sirin, a phrase I do not remember, is that he said: Even if he had the women of the people of the earth, then he said: All of these are gone."
"11034","From Mamar, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, he said: A man came to Ibn Masud and said: I divorced my wife ninety-nine times, and I asked and it was said to me: She has become separated from me. Ibn Masud said: They wished to separate you from her. He said: What do you say, may Allah have mercy on you, thinking he would grant him a concession. He said: Three separate her from you, and the rest is transgression."
"11035","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever divorces his wife thrice, she is divorced, and he has disobeyed his Lord."
"11036","From Ismail ibn Abdullah, he said: Ubaydullah ibn al-Ayzar informed me that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab, when he seized a man who had divorced his wife thrice, would strike his head painfully with the stick."
"11037","From Mamar, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, he said: When Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who divorces his wife thrice, he said: Had you feared Allah He would have made for you a way out, and he would add nothing to that."
"11038","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Mujahid, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who divorced his wife as many as the stars. He said: The head of al-Jawza suffices him of that."
"11039","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Rafi informed me, from Ata after his death, that a man said to Ibn Abbas: A man divorced his wife a hundred times. Ibn Abbas said: He takes three of that and leaves ninety-seven. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Kathir and al-Araj informed me, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it."
"11040","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ikrima ibn Khalid informed me that Said ibn Jubayr informed him that a man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I divorced my wife a thousand times. He said: Take three and leave nine hundred and ninety-seven. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Mujahid said, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it."
"11041","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Mujahid said, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man said to him: O Abu Abbas, I divorced my wife thrice. Ibn Abbas said: One of you divorces then acts foolishly, then says: O Abu Abbas. You disobeyed your Lord and parted from your wife. And Mujahid mentioned it, from his father, from Ibn Abbas."
"11042","From al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Murra, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I divorced my wife a thousand times. Ibn Abbas said: Three make her unlawful to you, and the rest is a sin upon you. You have taken the signs of Allah in mockery."
"11043","From Mamar, from a man, from al-Hasan and Qatada, about a man who said to his wife: You are divorced, you are divorced, he said: I only meant to make her understand. They both said: He is to be held to his oath."
"11044","From al-Thawri, about a man who said to his wife: You are divorced, you are divorced, then said: I meant only one, I only repeated to her to make her hear, he said: As for intention it is one, but as for judgment it binds him. It is the same if he says: You are divorced, you are divorced, it is in that same position."
"11045","From Sufyan, about a man who said to his wife: You are divorced thrice except thrice, he said: She is divorced from him thrice. And when he says: You are divorced thrice except twice, she is divorced once. And when he says: You are divorced thrice except once, she is divorced twice."
"11046","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man says to his wife: You are unlawful to me. He said: It is an oath. Then he recited: O Prophet, why do you forbid. I said: Even if he intended divorce and knew the place of divorce. He said: And if he says: You are to me like blood or like swine flesh, it is like his saying: She is unlawful to me."
"11047","From Mamar, from Qatada, he said: If he says: She is to me like blood or like swine flesh, it is like his saying: She is unlawful to me."
"11048","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed me, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: It is an oath."
"11049","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir and Ayyub, from Ikrima, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: It is an oath."
"11050","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, that Umar and Ibn Abbas said: It is an oath."
"11051","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Ibn Abbas said: It is an oath."
"11052","I heard Umar ibn Rashid narrating, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It is an oath. He said: And Ibn Abbas said: There was for you in the Messenger of Allah a good example."
"11053","From Muhammad ibn Rashid, that he heard Makhul saying the like of the saying of Ibn Abbas: It is an oath, and he said: There was for you in the Messenger of Allah a good example."
"11054","From Mamar, from Asim, from al-Shabi, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took an oath along with prohibition, so Allah reproached him for the prohibition and made for him the expiation of oath. Mamar said: As for Qatada, he said: He declared her unlawful so it was an oath."
"11055","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that Ibn Masud said: It is an oath which he expiates. As for al-Thawri, he mentioned it from Ashath, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that Ibn Masud said: If he intended divorce then it is divorce, otherwise it is an oath."
"11056","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: If he intended divorce it is divorce, and if he did not intend divorce it is an oath."
"11057","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: If he intended divorce it is one."
"11058","From Mamar, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: If he intended one it is one, and if he intended three it is three."
"11059","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: Our companions used to say about the unlawful: his intention counts. If he intended three it is three, and if he intended one it is one, irrevocable, and she has more right to herself, and if he wishes he may propose to her in the unlawful case."
"11060","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Whatever he intended, and it is not less than one."
"11061","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from al-Zuhri, that Zayd ibn Thabit said: It is three."
"11062","From Mamar, from Umar, and from al-Hasan, he said: If he intended three as divorce it is divorce, otherwise it is an oath."
"11063","From Mamar, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, he said: If he says: Everything lawful is unlawful to me, it is an oath, and Qatada used to give fatwa by it."
"11064","From Mamar, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Shabi, that Masruq said: I do not care whether I declared her unlawful or declared a bowl of tharid unlawful."
"11065","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim informed me, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he said: I do not care whether I declared her unlawful or declared river water unlawful."
"11066","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I do not care whether I declared her unlawful or declared a village unlawful."
"11067","From al-Thawri, from Salih ibn Muslim, from al-Shabi, he said: If he says: You are unlawful to me, it is lighter to me than my sandal."
"11068","From Mamar, from Qatada, from a man who heard Ali, he said about a mans saying: You are unlawful to me: She is made unlawful until she marries another husband."
"11069","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Ali, that he said about a man who says to his wife: You are unlawful to me, he said: It is three."
"11070","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from Qatada, from Khilas ibn Amr, that Adi ibn Qays, one of Banu Kilab, made his wife unlawful to himself. Ali ibn Abi Talib said to him: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you touch her before she marries another than you, I shall stone you."
"11071","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, he said: I heard al-Hasan and al-Hakam ibn Utayba both saying: It is three."
"11072","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, that Ali and Zayd separated between a man and his wife. He said: She is unlawful to me. And al-Hasan said it also."
"11073","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, he said: I heard him saying: I am the most knowledgeable of you of what Ali said about the unlawful. He said: I do not command you to go forward, nor do I command you to hold back."
"11074","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, about the unlawful, he said: Freeing a slave, or fasting two consecutive months, or feeding sixty poor."
"11075","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, the like of the hadith of al-Thawri. He said: Ibn Abbas said to me: A strongly emphasized oath."
"11076","From Mamar, from Khusayf, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, from Wahb, they said: It is in the position of zihar. When he says: She is unlawful to me: freeing a slave, or fasting two consecutive months, or feeding sixty poor. From Bakkar, from Wahb, the like of it."
"11077","From Mamar, from Qatada, about a man who said: His wife is unlawful to him like his mother, he said: It is zihar."
"11078","From al-Thawri, he said: He says about the unlawful in three ways: If he intended divorce it is upon what he intended, if he intended three it is three, if he intended one it is one irrevocable, if he intended an oath it is an oath, and if he intended nothing it is a lie and there is no expiation in it."
"11079","From al-Thawri, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim, he said: A man who had parted from his wife with two divorces was brought before Umar, then he said: You are unlawful to me. He said: I would never return her to him ever."
"11080","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man swears by divorce or other than it over a matter not to do it, then does it forgetfully, he said: I see nothing upon him. And Amr said the like of that."
"11081","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim told me that the companions of Ibn Masud used to bind him with that."
"11082","From Mamar, from Ibn Abi Najih, about a man who makes emancipation conditional on a matter then forgets, he used to see it as nothing, and divorce likewise."
"11083","From Mamar, he said: Ibn Khuthaym informed me, and I asked for him Said ibn Jubayr and Mujahid, and both of them freed her, then I asked Ata ibn Abi Rabah, and he said: If he wishes he makes her deferred in emancipation."
"11084","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada, about forgetfulness in divorce and emancipation, they both said: It is binding upon him. Mamar said: And al-Hasan said it also."
"11085","From Mamar, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jahshi, he said: A man forgot and said: His wife is divorced if there is in his house a dinar or a dirham, then afterwards he remembered a dinar that was in his house, so Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz separated between them."
"11086","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that he used to see it as nothing. He said: There is no breach of oath upon him."
"11087","From Mamar, from Qatada, about a man who had two dinars and swore by his wifes divorce that they were gone, then found one of them, he said: His wife is not divorced because they did not both go. But if he says: She is divorced if they have not gone, and he finds one of them, his wife is gone."
"11088","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I asked him about a man whom the ruler forces to divorce in a matter in which he is unjust to him, he said: There is no harm upon him to swear."
"11089","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he used to say: Swearing by divorce is false, it is nothing. I said: Did he see it as an oath. He said: I do not know."
"11090","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: Coerced divorce is not allowed."
"11091","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Abu al-Shatha said: Coerced divorce is nothing. From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Ata and Tawus, the like of that."
"11092","From al-Thawri, from Imran, from al-Hasan, and he was asked about that, and he said: They are the ones who divorced, and he did not see it as anything."
"11093","From Mamar, from one who heard al-Hasan saying: Coerced divorce is not allowed."
"11094","From Mamar, from Ismail ibn Abi Umayya, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz did not see it as anything."
"11095","From Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibn Abbas: He did not see coerced divorce as anything."
"11096","From Mamar, from Ayyub, that Ibn al-Zubayr did not see it as anything."
"11097","From Ubaydullah ibn Umar, that Thabit informed him that Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd died and left mothers of children. He said: So I proposed to one of them to Usayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, and he is younger than Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, and he married me to her. When that reached Abdullah he sent to me and I was brought to him, and behold iron and whips. He said: Divorce her or I shall strike you with these whips, or I shall bind you with this iron. He said: When I saw that I divorced her thrice, or he said: I made it decisive. Then I asked every jurist in Madina, and they said: It is nothing. Then I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: Go to Ibn al-Zubayr. He said: So I and Ibn Umar met at Ibn al-Zubayr in Makka, and I related to them, and they returned her to me."
"11098","From Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Thabit, freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab, informed him that he married a concubine of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd. He said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd met me and stepped on my foot. He said: And Thabit was lame. He said: He almost broke my foot. He said: I shall not move from you until you divorce her thrice. He said: So I divorced her thrice, and I had not consummated with her. He said: So I asked Ibn Umar, and he forbade me from her, that I propose to her. Then I asked Ibn al-Zubayr, and he said: Marry her if you wish. He said: So I mentioned that to Ibn Umar, and he said: I thought he would command you with that. Then I informed Ibn Umar that I had not consummated with her, and he said: Marry her if you wish."
"11099","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Said, from Thabit the lame, that he was imprisoned until he divorced, then I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: It is nothing."
"11100","From Ibn Uyayna, from Yahya ibn Said, from Thabit the lame, he said: I married a woman, I think he said: a mother of a child of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd. He said: His sons seized me and tied me until they almost crushed my foot, and said: We shall never release you until you divorce her. He said: So I divorced her, then I came to Ibn Umar and asked him, and he said: Your divorce is nothing."
"11101","From Hammad ibn Salama, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed me, from al-Hasan, from Ali: that he used to not see coerced divorce as anything. Abd al-Wahhab informed me of it. As for al-Thawri, he narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from one who heard Ali saying: All divorce is allowed except the divorce of the imbecile."
"11102","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abis ibn Rabia, from Ali, he said: Every divorce is allowed except the divorce of the imbecile."
"11103","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pardoned for this nation are mistake, forgetfulness, and what they were coerced to."
"11104","From Mamar, from Qatada, he narrates it: Three, he said: The son of Adam is not ruined by them: mistake, forgetfulness, and what he was coerced to."
"11105","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, he said: It reached Said ibn Jubayr that al-Hasan used to say: Coerced divorce is nothing. He said: May Allah have mercy on him. The people of idolatry used to coerce a man to disbelief and divorce, so that is nothing. But what the people of Islam do among themselves is allowed."
"11106","From al-Thawri, from Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, and from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, they both said: Coerced divorce is allowed. He only ransomed himself with it."
"11107","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada, they both said: Coerced divorce is allowed."
"11108","From Mamar, from Ayyub, that Ibn Umar said: Coerced divorce is allowed."
"11109","From al-Thawri and Ibn Uyayna, from Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, he said: If robbers coerce him it is not divorce, but if the ruler coerces him it is allowed. Ibn Uyayna said: They say: The thief advances to kill him, while the ruler does not kill him."
"11110","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Shurayh, he said: Fetters are coercion, threat is coercion, and prison is coercion."
"11111","From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from Ali ibn Hanzala, from his father, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: A man is not trustworthy over himself when you pain him, or bind him, or beat him."
"11112","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, and Jabir, from al-Shabi, about a man who divorces or emancipates in sleep, they both said: It is nothing. And Mamar said it, from al-Zuhri, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba."
"11113","From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from a man, from Ali, he said: A man came to him and said: This one claims he had a wet dream with my mother. He said: Go and make him stand in the sun and strike his shadow."
"11114","From Mamar, from al-Amash, from Abu Zabyan, that Ali said: The pen is lifted from the sleeper until he wakes. Umar said: You spoke the truth."
"11115","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: His divorce and his emancipation in his mind are nothing."
"11116","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: A man divorced his wife in his mind and it was taken from him. Abu al-Shatha said: He has divorced."
"11117","From Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, that he heard a man mentioning to Said ibn Jubayr: a cousin of his, and that Satan whispers to him of divorcing her. Said ibn Jubayr said to him: There is no harm upon you from that until you speak it or call witness to it."
"11118","From Mamar, from al-Hasan and Qatada, they both said: Whoever divorces his wife in his mind, that divorce of his is nothing."
"11119","From Mamar: A man asked al-Hasan and said: I divorced my wife in my mind. He said: Did anything come out of your mouth. He said: No. He said: It is nothing. He said: And he asked Qatada, and he said to him the like of the saying of al-Hasan. He said: Then Ibn Sirin was asked, and he said: Has Allah not known what is in your mind. He said: Yes. He said: I say nothing about it."
"11120","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When he writes to her of her divorce, divorce has fallen upon her. If he denies her he is made to swear."
"11121","From al-Thawri, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, about a man who writes of divorce but does not utter it, and does not see it as complete, he said: It is allowed."
"11122","From al-Thawri, he said: Ibn Abi Layla informed me, from al-Hakam, he said: Writing is speech: Then He revealed to them to glorify morning and evening. He said: He wrote to them."
"11123","From Mamar, from a man, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, he said: When he writes it, it is binding, even if he utters nothing."
"11124","From Mamar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from al-Shabi, he said: When he writes to her of her divorce and does not utter it, then erases it before it reaches her, it is not divorce so long as it does not reach her. Mamar said: And one who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying the like of the saying of al-Shabi."
"11125","From Mamar, from Qatada, he said: When he writes it and does not utter it, then hands it to a man and says: Deliver, O so-and-so, this to so-and-so, it is binding upon him. But if he erases it before handing it, it is nothing."
"11126","From Mamar, he said: And one who heard Ikrima informed me, saying: When a man wants to write to his wife of her divorce, let him write to her: When this letter of mine comes to you and you become pure from your menstruation, then observe waiting period."
"11127","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, he said: Al-Shabi was asked about a man who traced his wifes divorce on a pillow. He said: It is binding upon him."
"11128","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who divorces his wife then denies her the divorce, he said: He is made to swear, and she is returned to him."
"11129","From Mamar, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, he said: He is made to swear, then the sin is upon him. He said: And Qatada said: He is made to swear between the Corner and the Station."
"11130","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin and others, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: She flees from him as much as she can, and ransoms herself from him with all she can."
"11131","From al-Thawri, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: When he denies her the divorce, they are two adulterers so long as they stay together."
"11132","From Mamar and al-Thawri, they both said: She flees from him as much as she can, and does not perfume herself, and does not adorn herself, and flees from him. Mamar said: And she disobeys his command, and he does not touch her except while she is unwilling."
"11133","From Mamar, from Qatada, he said: When she claims divorce against him and he denies her, then he stays with her until he dies, she does not inherit from him."
"11134","From Mamar, he said: And I heard other than Qatada saying: She is asked at his death. If she stands by her word she does not inherit from him, but if she introduces something she is made to swear and inherits. And it is more beloved to Mamar."
"11135","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Ata saying: Ibn Abbas said: There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership. Ata said: If he swears by the divorce of what he has not married, it is nothing. And Ibn Abbas used to say: Divorce is only after marriage, and likewise emancipation."
"11136","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Ala, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Marwan asked him about a relative of his who specified a woman: if he marries her she is divorced. Ibn Abbas said: There is no divorce until you marry, and no emancipation until you own."
"11137","From Mamar, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabra, from Ali, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: No suckling after weaning, no continuous fasting, no orphanhood after puberty, no silence a day to night, and no divorce before marriage. Al-Thawri said to him: O Abu Urwa, it is only from Ali, halted. But Mamar refused him except from the Prophet."
"11138","From al-Thawri, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from al-Nazzal ibn Sabra, from Ali, he said: No suckling after weaning, no orphanhood after puberty, no silence a day to night, and no divorce before marriage."
"11139","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: There is no divorce before marriage."
"11140","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Dumayra, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali, he said: There is no divorce before marriage even if he names her."
"11141","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Mubarak, from al-Hasan, he said: A man asked Ali, he said: I said: If I marry so-and-so she is divorced. Ali said: It is nothing."
"11142","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Tawus, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no divorce before marriage, and no vow in what one does not own."
"11143","From Mamar, from Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: There is no divorce in what you do not own, and no emancipation in what you do not own."
"11144","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from one who heard Tawus narrating, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no divorce for one who has not married, and no emancipation for one who has not owned."
"11145","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Tawus, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no divorce before marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership."
"11146","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr informed me that he was with Ibn al-Musayyab when the messenger of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz came to him and said: What do you think about a man who said: My wife is divorced, and every woman I marry is divorced. Ibn al-Musayyab said: If he broke his oath, his wife is divorced. As for what he has not married, there is no divorce until he marries."
"11147","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim al-Jazari informed me that he asked Said ibn al-Musayyab, Said ibn Jubayr, and Ata ibn Abi Rabah about a mans divorce of what he has not married. They said: There is no divorce before he marries, whether he names her or does not name her."
"11148","From Mamar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, that he asked Said ibn al-Musayyab, Said ibn Jubayr, and Ata ibn Abi Rabah, and all of them said: There is no divorce before marriage."
"11149","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Amr ibn Shuayb mentioning that he asked more than one of the elders of the people of Madina, and he named them but I do not remember any of them, except that I think among them Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salama, and all of them said: There is no divorce before marriage."
"11150","From Ibn Jurayj, from Uthman ibn Umara, that he heard Ibn al-Musayyab saying: There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership."
"11151","From Ibn Jurayj and Mamar, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, he said: There is no divorce before marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership. Ibn Jurayj added and said: Whoever divorces what he has not married, or emancipates what he has not owned, that saying of his is false."
"11152","From Mamar, from al-Hasan and Qatada, they both said: There is no divorce before marriage, and no emancipation before ownership."
"11153","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: There is no divorce before marriage."
"11154","From Mamar, he said: It reached me from Shurayh that he said: There is no divorce before marriage."
"11155","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: It reached Ibn Abbas that Ibn Masud says: If he divorces what he has not married it is allowed. Ibn Abbas said: He erred in this. Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: When you marry believing women then divorce them before you touch them, and He did not say: When you divorce believing women then marry them."
"11156","From Mamar, he said: Al-Walid ibn Yazid wrote to his governor in Sanaa to ask those with him about divorce before marriage. He said: Ibn Tawus was asked and narrated to them, from his father, that he said: There is no divorce before marriage. He said: And Abu al-Miqdam and Simak were asked, and Abu al-Miqdam narrated, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, and Simak, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, that they both said: There is no divorce before marriage. He said: And Simak said: Marriage is a knot that is tied, and divorce unties it, so how is a knot untied before it is tied. So he wrote with his saying, and it pleased them, and he wrote that he appoint a judge over Yemen."
"11157","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Qays, he said: I asked Ibrahim and al-Shabi about divorce before marriage. They both said: al-Aswad named a woman, and specified: if he marries her she is divorced. He asked about that Ibn Masud, and he said: She has separated from you, so propose to her for yourself."
"11158","From al-Thawri, from Mansur and al-Amash, from Ibrahim, he said: When he specifies a woman or a tribe it is allowed, but when he generalizes every woman it is nothing."
"11159","From Mamar, from Hammad, he said: When he specifies a woman or a tribe it is allowed, but when he generalizes it is nothing. Ibrahim said it. Al-Thawri, from Zakariyya, and Ismail, from al-Shabi, the like of the saying of Ibrahim."
"11160","From Yasin, from Abu Muhammad, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, that a man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: Every woman I marry is divorced thrice. Umar said to him: It is as you said."
"11161","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who said: Every woman I marry is divorced, and every slave girl I buy is free, he said: It is as he said. Mamar said: So I said: Has it not come from some of them that he said: There is no divorce before marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership. He said: That is only that a man says: The wife of so-and-so is divorced, and the slave of so-and-so is free."
"11162","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Is zihar that he says: She is to me like my mother. He said: Yes, it is what Allah the Exalted mentioned: Those who do zihar of their women."
"11163","From Mamar, from Qatada, about His saying: Then they return to what they said, he said: He made her upon him like the back of his mother, then he returns and does zihar, so freeing a slave."
"11164","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, about His saying: Then they return to what they said, he said: The one who has intercourse, when he speaks the reprehensible and false zihar and breaks it, upon him is the expiation."
"11165","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: The divorce of the people of ignorance was zihar, and a man did zihar in Islam while intending divorce, so Allah sent down about him the expiation."
"11166","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Whoever declares zihar with a female mahram, a blood relative, or a foster sister through suckling, all of that is like his mother; she is not lawful for him until he expiates."
"11167","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Whoever declares zihar and likens his wife to a woman whom it is unlawful for him to marry, we hold that he must perform the expiation of zihar."
"11168","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: Whoever declares zihar with a female mahram, it is zihar."
"11169","From Ma'mar, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, he said: Whoever declares zihar with a female mahram, a sister, a maternal aunt, or a paternal aunt, it is zihar."
"11170","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Whoever declares zihar with any female mahram, it is zihar; he mentioned it from Abu Ishaq and Muhammad ibn Salim."
"11171","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: Whoever declares zihar with a female mahram, it is zihar."
"11172","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata was asked about a man who declared zihar with his maternal uncle's daughter; he said: It is not zihar; zihar is only with female mahrams."
"11173","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What if a man says, If I do such and such then my wife is upon me like my mother, then he does it; he said: That is zihar."
"11174","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: If he breaks his oath then zihar is incumbent upon him, and if he does not break it then there is nothing."
"11175","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: If he declares zihar with other than women, with food or drink or any deed whatever it is, then if he does it, he expiates for his oath."
"11176","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, that he said: When a man forbids himself food from eating it, then eats it, he expiates for his oath."
"11177","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: When a man forbids himself food from eating it, then eats it, he expiates for his oath."
"11178","From Ma'mar, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, he said: Whoever forbids food, it is nothing, and there is no expiation upon him; and he mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took an oath along with the prohibition."
"11179","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Before they touch one another; he said: Intercourse itself."
"11180","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr and Abd al-Karim, the like of the saying of Ata: Intercourse itself."
"11181","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada, they both said: Intercourse itself."
"11182","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I said to him: What is lawful for the one who declared zihar from his wife before he expiates? He said: He may kiss and touch; only that they touch one another was mentioned. I said: May he fulfill his need without her private part? He said: I do not see anything harms him except intercourse itself. I said: Do you not treat her like the woman who is divorced as long as she is not taken back? He said: No."
"11183","From Ma'mar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about a man who declared zihar with his wife: May he see her hair, or may she uncover herself before him before he expiates? He said: There is no harm in it; he was only forbidden intercourse until he expiates."
"11184","From al-Thawri, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm if the one who declared zihar touches and kisses."
"11185","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Freeing, feeding, and fasting in zihar, all of that is before they touch one another."
"11186","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada, they both said: Freeing in zihar, feeding, and fasting are before they touch one another."
"11187","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If he fasts until an hour of the two months remains, then he becomes able to free, he frees, as knowledge, not as opinion."
"11188","From Ma'mar, from Jabir, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, he said: When he becomes able to free a slave before he completes his fast, he frees."
"11189","From Ma'mar, from one who heard al-Hasan, saying: When he becomes able to free before he completes his fast, he frees."
"11190","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, concerning the one who declared zihar fasting then becoming able to free before he completes his fast, he said: The fasting collapses whenever he becomes able."
"11191","From al-Thawri, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, he said: When he fasts in the expiation of an oath, then finds the expiation, he feeds."
"11192","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada, they both said: When he fasts a month then becomes able for a slave, then if he wishes he continues his fast, and if he wishes he frees a slave."
"11193","From Abd Allah ibn Kathir, from Shu'ba, from al-Hakam and Hammad, they both said: When he fasts a month then becomes able for freeing before he completes the fasting, he frees. He said: And al-Hakam said: If I fasted fifty-eight days then became able, I would free."
"11194","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il, from al-Hasan or another, concerning the one who declared zihar fasting then having intercourse with his wife before he completes his fast, he said: The fast collapses. He said: And if he feeds some of the poor then has intercourse with his wife, it does not collapse, but let him feed the remainder."
"11195","From Ma'mar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about the man fasting a month in zihar then falling ill and breaking fast; he said: Let him restart. He said: I said to al-Zuhri: Then he broke fast on a cloudy day, then the sun appeared; he said: He replaces a day in its place."
"11196","From Ma'mar, he said: And I asked Ata al-Khurasani, and he said: We used to deem it like the month of Ramadan until we wrote about it to our brothers among the people of Kufa, and they wrote to us that he restarts. Ma'mar said: And al-Hakam ibn Utayba used to say: He restarts."
"11197","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, he said: He restarts his fasting."
"11198","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from a man, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: He restarts."
"11199","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: He makes up, and does not restart."
"11200","From al-Thawri, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Consecutive, as Allah said; he says: If he breaks fast between them, he restarts; and Sufyan holds this."
"11201","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Mujahid, he said: Every fasting in the Quran is consecutive except the making up of Ramadan."
"11202","From Ma'mar, from al-Hasan and Qatada, they both used to permit in that when he had an excuse, and they both say: He makes up."
"11203","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, he said: When he falls ill and breaks fast, he makes up, and does not restart."
"11204","From Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, concerning the man fasting the two consecutive months then falling ill, he said: He completes upon what has passed, and does not restart. It was said to Ma'mar: He puts the month of Ramadan or the day of sacrifice between them; he said: It enters into the saying of these and these."
"11205","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If he puts the month of Ramadan or the day of sacrifice between them, he has not kept continuity then; he says: He restarts."
"11206","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, and Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Ibrahim ibn Maysara, from Tawus, he said: When he falls ill, he completes upon what has passed, and does not restart."
"11207","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When the one who declared zihar fasts from the beginning of the crescent, he fasts two months, whether they are sixty days, fifty-nine days, or fifty-eight days; and when he does not fast from the beginning of the crescent, he counts sixty days."
"11208","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: It was said to Ata while I was listening: A man declared zihar with his wife and did not expiate until he had intercourse with her; evil is what he did, let him seek Allah's forgiveness, then let him keep away from her until he expiates. I said: Is there any hadd or anything upon him? He said: I know of none."
"11209","From Ma'mar, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: One expiation. Ma'mar said: And al-Hasan said it also."
"11210","From al-Thawri, from Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, and Yunus, from al-Hasan, they both said: One expiation, and he seeks forgiveness of his Lord."
"11211","From Ma'mar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrima the freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man declared zihar with his wife then had intercourse with her before he expiated, and he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: And what drove you to that? He said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Messenger of Allah, I saw her anklets, or he said: her legs, in the moonlight, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Then keep away from her until you do what Allah the Exalted commanded you; from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hakam, from Ikrima, the like of it."
"11212","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ibn Ajlan, from Ibn Qusayit, from Ibn al-Musayyib: That a man declared zihar with his wife, then had intercourse with her before he expiated, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him with one expiation."
"11213","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Salman ibn Sakhr al-Ansari, that he made his wife upon him like the back of his mother until Ramadan passes, then she became plump and fleshy, so he had intercourse with her in the middle of Ramadan, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as if magnifying that, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Can you free a slave? He said: No. He said: Then can you fast two consecutive months? He said: No. He said: Then can you feed sixty poor? He said: No. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Farwa ibn Amr, give him that irq, and it is a basket, taking fifteen sa' or sixteen sa', so let him feed it to sixty poor. He said: Upon one poorer than me? By the One Who sent you with the truth, there is no household between her two lava fields more needy of it than me. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, then said: Go with it to your family."
"11214","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: He feeds them all together; it is not proper that he separates them."
"11215","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Two expiations are upon him."
"11216","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Qabisa ibn Dhuwayb, he said: Two expiations, and Qatada used to give fatwa with it."
"11217","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man declared zihar with his wife then he died, or she died, and he did not expiate? He said: She is his wife, they inherit one another, and there is no expiation."
"11218","From Ma'mar, from Hafs ibn Abi Sulayman and others, from al-Hasan, he said: Concerning the one who declared zihar when one of them dies, he said: He inherits her, and there is no expiation upon him."
"11219","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: He inherits her and there is no expiation upon him, and his reckoning is upon his Lord."
"11220","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: He expiates then he inherits from him."
"11221","From Abd Allah ibn Kathir, from Shu'ba, from al-Hakam, from al-Sha'bi, he said: He expiates and inherits her. Al-Hakam said, and Ibrahim said: They inherit one another, and there is no expiation upon him."
"11222","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man declared zihar with his wife, then did not expiate until he divorced her, then her waiting period ended, then she married and was consummated with, then her husband divorced her or died from her, then her first husband returned to her; he said: Then he shall not touch her until he expiates."
"11223","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who declared zihar with his wife, then divorced her thrice, then she married and he died from her or divorced her, then her first husband wanted to marry her, he said: The expiation of zihar is upon him."
"11224","From al-Thawri, concerning the one who declared zihar divorcing before he expiates then taking back, he said: He shall not have intercourse with her until he expiates."
"11225","From Uthman, from Sa'id, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, he said: He shall not have intercourse with her until he expiates."
"11226","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: When he declares zihar with his wife, then divorces her, then leaves her until her waiting period ends, then she marries another and he dies from her or divorces her, then her first husband returns to her, he said: There is no expiation of zihar upon him. He said: And Qatada also used to narrate the like of this saying from al-Hasan. Ma'mar said: As for Matar al-Warraq, he mentioned from al-Hasan: That the expiation of zihar is upon him."
"11227","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who swears triple divorce upon his wife that she shall not enter the house of so-and-so, then divorces her once, until when her waiting period ends he marries her, then she enters the house which he swore she would not enter, al-Hasan did not deem it anything when that is after separation and marriage; he says: His saying was demolished by the separation. And Qatada used to give fatwa with this."
"11228","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, that he used to make binding the likes of this."
"11229","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who says to his wife: If you leave this house of mine then you are divorced thrice, then divorces her once, until when her waiting period ends she leaves, he said: I do not deem that he should propose to her, nor marry her, until she marries another husband."
"11230","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swears divorce that she shall not enter a house, then divorces his wife, then leaves her until the waiting period passes, then she enters the house, then he marries her, he said: No harm; the oath-breaking occurred, and she is not his wife; and if she enters the house after he marries her, when she had become distinct from him by the first divorce, there is no harm upon him also."
"11231","From Ma'mar, from Matar al-Warraq, from al-Hasan and Ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man who says to his wife: If you do such and such then she is divorced once or twice, then she does not do that until he divorces her thrice, and she marries another husband and he consummates with her, then divorces her, then her first husband marries her and she does what he mentioned, they said: No oath-breaking falls upon him, because the three demolish what was before them."
"11232","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I asked him about a man who declares zihar with a woman before he marries her, then marries her; he said: He expiates before he touches her."
"11233","From Ma'mar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ibn al-Musayyib, concerning a man who declares zihar with a woman he has not married, then marries her, he said: The expiation of zihar is upon him."
"11234","From Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, the like of it; he said: The expiation of zihar is upon him."
"11235","From Malik, from Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad: That a man made a woman upon him like the back of his mother if he marries her, so he asked Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said: If he marries her then let him not approach her until he expiates."
"11236","From al-Thawri, concerning zihar before marriage, he said: Zihar falls upon him."
"11237","From Ma'mar, from al-Hasan and Qatada, they both said: If he declares zihar before he marries then it is nothing, except that he marries."
"11238","From Ibn Uyayna, from Ibn Ajlan, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that he did not deem zihar before marriage anything, nor divorce before marriage anything."
"11239","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If he declares zihar with a woman repeatedly, then one expiation."
"11240","From Ma'mar, from Qatada and Amr ibn Dinar, they both say: When he declares zihar in one sitting repeatedly, then one expiation is upon him, and if he declares zihar in separate sittings then separate expiations; and oaths are likewise."
"11241","From Ma'mar, from a man, from al-Hasan, he said: When he declares zihar repeatedly, even if in separate sittings, then one expiation so long as he has not expiated; and oaths are likewise. From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, that he says the like of the saying of al-Hasan. Ma'mar said: And one who heard Ikrima and al-Hasan informed me, they both say the like of it in oaths, and it did not reach me what they both said in zihar."
"11242","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Tawus and Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, concerning the one who declares zihar repeatedly, they both said: One expiation, even if in separate sittings, then one expiation so long as he has not expiated."
"11243","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Layth, from Tawus, from al-Sha'bi, they both said: If he declared zihar fifty times, there is nothing upon him except one expiation."
"11244","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id, from Qatada, from Khilas ibn Amr, from Ali, he said: When he declares zihar repeatedly in one sitting then one expiation, and if he declares zihar in separate seats then separate expiations; and oaths are likewise."
"11245","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, Ali said: When a man declares zihar with his wife in separate sittings, then separate expiations are upon him, and if he declares zihar in one sitting repeatedly, then one expiation is upon him; and oaths are likewise."
"11246","From al-Thawri, he said: But we say: When he intends the first then one expiation, and if he intends to emphasize then for each oath an expiation; and oaths are likewise."
"11247","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I said to him: A man declares zihar with his wives, and says: You are upon him like his mother; he said: One expiation. Then if he says: So-and-so is upon him like his mother, and so-and-so is upon him like his mother, another in one utterance, then two expiations are upon him. Ibn Jurayj said: And I say: Take zihar by oaths. From Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, the like of the saying of Ata. From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, the like of the hadith of Ibn Jurayj from Ata in zihar."
"11248","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: A man with three wives came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and said: You are upon him like the back of his mother, so Umar said: One expiation."
"11249","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: That a man declared zihar with three wives in the time of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, so Umar said: One expiation."
"11250","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Tawus, he said: When he declares zihar with four wives then one expiation. He said: And al-Hakam said: For each woman among them an expiation when he declares zihar with his wives."
"11251","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When he declares zihar with four wives, then four expiations."
"11252","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, he said: When he declares zihar with his wives then for each one an expiation. And other than Qatada said, from al-Hasan: One expiation suffices him for them."
"11253","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: For the one who declared zihar four months pass; he said: That is not ila'. It was said to him: That you are admonished thereby is a punishment. Then he said: In ila' separately. He said: And he said to me in zihar what he said, and he differentiated between them."
"11254","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from a man, from Ali, that he said: No ila' enters into zihar, and no zihar into ila'."
"11255","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning the one who declared zihar when four months pass for him, he said: That is not ila'; whenever he expiates then she is his wife. Ma'mar said: And one who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying with what al-Zuhri said: There is no time limit for him."
"11256","From al-Thawri, from Dawud, he said: I asked al-Sha'bi about a man who says: His wife is upon him like the back of his mother; he said: Ila' is not zihar, and zihar is not ila'."
"11257","From Abd Allah ibn Muharrar, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, he said: There is no time limit for zihar; whenever he expiates then she is his wife."
"11258","From Ma'mar, from Asim, from Jabir ibn Zayd Abu al-Sha'tha: Concerning a man who declares zihar with his wife, then leaves her until four months pass, then it is ila'."
"11259","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: It is ila'."
"11260","As for Uthman ibn Matar, he mentioned, from Sa'id, from Qatada, from al-Hasan and Ibn al-Musayyib, that they both said: There is no time limit for zihar; whenever he expiates then she is his wife."
"11261","From al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilaba, he said: Their divorce in the Jahiliyya was zihar and ila', so Allah made in zihar what you heard, and made in ila' what you heard."
"11262","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said to me: When the one who declared zihar keeps his oath, he does not expiate."
"11263","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: When the one who declared zihar keeps his oath, he does not expiate."
"11264","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, he said: The one who declared zihar expiates even if he keeps his oath."
"11265","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: The one who declared zihar expiates even if he keeps his oath; he has uttered an evil word and a falsehood."
"11266","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, concerning the man who declares zihar with his slave girl before he touches her, he said: He expiates the expiation of a free woman if he intends to tread her. From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada, the like of the saying of Ibn Tawus."
"11267","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who declares zihar with his slave girl, then intends to marry her, he said: If he wishes he frees her, and makes her freeing the expiation of his oath, but let him advance something to her."
"11268","From al-Thawri, from Hammad and Mughira, from Ibrahim, he said: Whoever declares zihar with his slave girl, then it is zihar, so let him expiate. Hammad said, and Ibrahim said: Even if he has not touched her, when she is in his possession then let him not touch her until he expiates."
"11269","From Ma'mar, from Matar al-Warraq, from al-Hasan, he said: When he does not touch her then there is no expiation upon him."
"11270","From al-Thawri, from Abu Najih, from Mujahid, he said: The expiation of the slave girl and the free woman is a complete expiation."
"11271","From al-Thawri, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: They are of the women."
"11272","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Al-Hakam ibn Aban informed me, from Ikrima the freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: He expiates the like of the expiation of a free woman. And Amr ibn Dinar said it."
"11273","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man declares zihar with his slave girl; he said: As for me, I would expiate half the expiation of a free woman, as her waiting period is half the waiting period of a free woman."
"11274","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who declares zihar with his concubine, he did not deem it zihar; Allah the Exalted said: And those who declare zihar among their wives."
"11275","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a woman who says to her husband: He is upon her like her father, he said: She has uttered an evil word and a falsehood, so we deem that she expiate by freeing a slave, or fasting two consecutive months, or feeding sixty poor, and this saying of hers does not prevent her husband from treading her."
"11276","From al-Thawri, he said: Al-Hasan used not to deem her zihar with her husband zihar."
"11277","From Ibn Jurayj, her declaring zihar, she says: He is upon her like her father; he said: It is an oath, it is not zihar; she forbade what Allah made lawful to him."
"11278","From Sufyan al-Thawri, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, that A'isha bint Talha declared zihar with Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr if she marries him, so fatwa was sought for her from many jurists, and they ordered her to expiate, so she freed a slave boy of hers worth two thousand. From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, and Ash'ath, from Ibn Sirin, the like of this."
"11279","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim informed me, from a freedman of A'isha bint Talha, that Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr proposed to her, and she said: He is upon me like my father. Then when he was over Iraq he proposed to her, and she said: Veil this Bedouin from me, for he is upon me like my father. Then she sought fatwa in Medina, and she was given fatwa to expiate for her oath and marry him."
"11280","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Shubruma, he said: The daughter of Talha said, I think he said: Fatima, to Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr, if she marries him then he is upon her like her father, then she married him, so he asked about that the companions of Ibn Mas'ud, and they said: She expiates. Ma'mar said: And I did not hear anyone before us deem it anything, among them al-Hasan and Qatada, they both said: It is not zihar."
"11281","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, he said: If the one who declared zihar says: I have no need of her, he is not left until he divorces or takes back."
"11282","From al-Thawri, he said: It reached me, from Ata or Ibrahim, that he used to say: When he declares zihar with her for an hour then it binds him. And Ibn Abi Layla said it. And another said: When he declares zihar for an hour then the hour passes, it is nothing; and it is our saying."
"11283","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about ila', and he said: That he swears by Allah not to have intercourse with her, or that he will anger her, or harm her, or forbid her, or his head and her head shall not meet. Al-Thawri said: As for when he says: I will not approach you, and I will not touch you, then it is nothing until it is an oath."
"11284","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Ila' is that he swears by Allah upon intercourse itself for more than four months, whether he strikes a term or does not strike, when what he swears upon is four months or more. Ata said: As for that he says I will not touch you, and does not swear, or says a grave word then deserts her, then it is not ila'."
"11285","From Abd Allah ibn Muharrar, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, that Abd Allah ibn Abbas said to him: How is Tahallul? Meaning his wife. My knowledge of her is sharp-tongued. He said: Yes, by Allah, I left and I do not speak to her. He said: Then hasten the journey before four months pass, for if four months pass then it is an irrevocable divorce, and you are a suitor."
"11286","From Ma'mar, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, he said: How is Tahallul? Meaning his wife. He said: My knowledge of her is sharp-tongued. He said: Yes, by Allah, I left and I do not speak to her. He said: Then hasten before four months pass, for if they pass then it is a divorce."
"11287","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, he said: Ila' is that he swears he will not touch her ever or less, when what he swears is more than four months."
"11288","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: When he swears by Allah he will not approach her, then leaves her until four months elapse, then it is ila', whether he strikes a term or does not strike. Then if he says: I will not approach you, I will not touch you, and deserts her, then that is not ila'."
"11289","Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us, that he heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Ila' is that he swears he will never come to her. From Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar said: That Abu Yahya, the freedman of Mu'adh, informed him, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it."
"11290","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Ya'qub informed me from you that you heard Ibn Abbas saying: If he names a term then he has the term, it is not ila', and if he does not name it then it is ila'. He said: I did not hear anything from Ibn Abbas in ila'. So I said: Then how do you say? He said: Whether he names a term or does not name, then when four months pass as Allah said, then it is one."
"11291","From Ma'mar, from Khusayf, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Every oath that intervenes between the man and his wife, it is ila': When he says: By Allah I will anger you, by Allah I will harm you, by Allah I will not approach you, and the likes of this."
"11292","From Hammad, from Ibrahim, and from Abd Allah ibn Abi Safar, from al-Shu'bi, he said: Every oath that prevents intercourse, it is ila'."
"11293","From al-Thawri, he said: But we say: When he intends the first then one expiation, and if he intends to emphasize then for each oath an expiation."
"11294","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a man who swears he will not speak to his wife, and he said: Ila' was only in intercourse, and I fear this is ila'."
"11295","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: When he swears by Allah that he will anger her, or harm her, or forbid her, or his head and her head shall not meet, then it is ila'."
"11296","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: It is not ila'; he has already angered her when he did not approach her."
"11297","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a man who swears he will not speak to his wife, and he said: Ila' was only in intercourse, and I fear this is ila'."
"11298","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Abu al-Sha'tha, he said: If he says: You are upon me forbidden, you are upon me like my mother, or you are divorced if I approach you, then it is ila', and every oath by which he swears he will not approach her, it is ila', when four months pass; and if he approaches her before them then he is upon what he said."
"11299","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If he swears he will not approach for a term he names less than four, then it is not ila'. From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, the like of it."
"11300","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata was asked about a man who swears he will not approach his wife a month, then stays from her five months; he said: That is not ila'."
"11301","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Tawus, concerning a man who swears he will not approach his wife three days, then leaves her three months, he said: That is not ila'. From al-Thawri, from a man, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, the like of it. From Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, the like of it."
"11302","From al-Thawri, from some of his companions, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It is not ila'. He mentioned it from Amir al-Ahwal."
"11303","I heard al-Hajjaj ibn Artat, asked about a man who swears he will not approach his wife ten days then leaves her four months, and he said: Al-Hakam informed me, from Ibrahim and others, that he said: It is the chapter of ila'."
"11304","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, the like of it; he said: It is ila'."
"11305","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata was asked about a man who swears he will not approach his wife a month, then stays from her five months; he said: That is ila', whether he names a term or does not name it, then when four months pass as Allah the Exalted said, then it is one."
"11306","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Wabara, from a man among them, he said: He took ila' from his wife ten days, then he asked about it Ibn Mas'ud, and he said: If four months pass then it is ila'."
"11307","From al-Thawri, he said: When he swears he will not approach his wife, and says: If Allah wills, then it is not ila'."
"11308","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swears he will not approach his wife in this year except once, then has intercourse with her after months, and the extent of what is between him and his falling upon her, and between the completion of the year, is more than four months, ila' falls upon him when he has intercourse with her. Then if there is not between him and the completion of the year except less than four months, ila' does not fall upon him. Indeed ila' only falls when he has intercourse with her."
"11309","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, that Sa'id ibn Jubayr informed him, he said: It reached me that Ali ibn Abi Talib, a man said to him: I swore I will not touch my wife two years, so he ordered him to keep away from her. Then the man said to him: That is only because she is nursing, so he left him with her."
"11310","From al-Thawri, he said: Simak ibn Harb informed me, from Abu Atiyya al-Hujaymi, he said: He swore he will not approach his wife until she weans his son Qa'nab. He said: Then he passed by the people and they said: How well Qa'nab was nourished. Then he informed them that he had taken ila' from her until she weans him. Then the people said: We do not deem your wife but distinct from you. Then he came to Ali and asked him about that, and he said: If you took the oath in your anger then your wife has become distinct from you, and if it was other than that then she is your wife."
"11311","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, that he asked him about a man whose wife was nursing, and he swore by divorce not to approach her until she weans her. He said: If he approaches her before four months pass, divorce has occurred, but if he leaves her until four months pass, it is ila."
"11312","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a man who swore not to approach his wife while she was nursing. He said: It is not ila; he only intended reform by it. Ma'mar said: And it reached me something similar from Ali."
"11313","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a man who swore by the divorce of his wife, three times, not to approach her for a year. He said: Qatadah said: Al-Hasan used to say: When the months pass, she has become separated from him, and if he marries her after that, there is no ila upon him; the divorce and the marriage have demolished it. He said: I said: Transmit it. Abu al-Sha'tha said: When the months pass, she has become separated from him, and if he marries her after that, there is no ila upon him, but he shall not approach her until the year passes, and if he touches her, he breaks his oath. Ma'mar said: And it reached me from Ibrahim that he said: If he marries her after that, ila has occurred."
"11314","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, he said: When the months pass, she has become separated from him, and if he marries her after that, he is still a mu'li. And if he does not touch her until the months pass, she has become separated from him, and if he marries her after that, he is still a mu'li. And if he does not touch her until the months pass, she becomes separated from him as well."
"11315","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, about a man who said to his wife: You are divorced if I touch you for five months. He said: That is not ila; divorce is not an oath so as to be ila."
"11316","From Ma'mar, from Ata al-Khurasani, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman heard me asking Ibn al-Musayyib about ila, then I passed by him and he said: What did he say to you? So I told him of it. He said: Shall I not tell you what Uthman ibn Affan and Zayd ibn Thabit used to say? I said: Yes. He said: They used to say: When four months pass, it is one, and she has more right to herself; she observes the waiting period of a divorced woman."
"11317","From Ma'mar and Ibn Uyaynah, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: Al-Nu'man took an ila oath from his wife, while he was sitting with Ibn Mas'ud, so he struck his thigh and said: When four months pass, then acknowledge one divorce."
"11318","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, he said: Yazid ibn al-Asamm informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: The expiry of the four is the determination of divorce, and fay' is intercourse."
"11319","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said: When the four months pass, it is one divorce, and she has more right to herself. Qatadah said: Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said: She observes the waiting period of a divorced woman. From Ibn Jurayj and al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, similar to the hadith of Abdullah ibn Muharrar."
"11320","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that Ibn Abbas used to recite: For those who swear from their wives, then if they resolve departure."
"11321","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Abbas said: When four months pass, it is one, and she has more right to herself."
"11322","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said: When four months pass, it is one, and she has more right to herself, and she observes the waiting period of a divorced woman."
"11323","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah: Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said: She observes the waiting period of a divorced woman after the four. Qatadah said, and Ibn Abbas said: Do not prolong it upon her; when the four pass, she may marry."
"11324","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abu al-Sha'tha used to say: When the four months pass, she has more control over her affair, and she does not observe a waiting period after it."
"11325","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: When the four months pass and he has not returned, it is one, and she has more right to herself, and she observes the waiting period of a divorced woman. And there is no inheritance between them, and she has no maintenance unless she is pregnant. And it is binding that he be seized at the expiry of the four, so he either returns or divorces; if he does not do so, it is one."
"11326","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Muslim informed me that he heard Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, saying: When the four pass, it is one divorce, and she has more right to herself."
"11327","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Dawud ibn Abi Asim narrating that Muhammad ibn Yusuf ordered him to ask about a woman of Thaqif from whom her husband took an ila oath. He listed men he asked about that, among them Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas; all of them said: When four months pass, it is an irrevocable divorce."
"11328","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, that Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb said: When four months pass, it is an irrevocable divorce. He said: And Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham said: It is one divorce, and he has more right to her. And al-Zuhri used to adopt the saying of Abu Bakr."
"11329","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me that Ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman said: When the months pass, it is one, and he has more right to her."
"11330","From Muhammad ibn Rashid, that he heard Makhul saying: When the four pass, it is one, and he has more right to her until she menstruates three menstruations. From al-Thawri, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Makhul, similar."
"11331","From Ma'mar, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The mu'li is stopped at the expiry of the four; he must either return or divorce."
"11332","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Marwan, from Ali, he said: When the four pass, he is detained until he returns or divorces."
"11333","From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from Amr ibn Salamah, from Ali: When the four pass, he is stopped until he returns or divorces."
"11334","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Abu al-Darda and Aishah said: The mu'li is stopped at the expiry of the four; he must either return or divorce."
"11335","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that a man took an ila oath from his wife, and Aishah said to him after twenty months: Has it not come time for you to return?"
"11336","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that a man used to take an ila oath from his wife for a year, then he would come to Aishah, and she would recite to him: For those who take an ila oath from their wives, and order him to fear Allah and to return."
"11337","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The mu'li is stopped at the expiry of the four; he must either return or divorce. From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, similar."
"11338","From Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, he said: The mu'li is stopped at the expiry of the four; he must either return or divorce."
"11339","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Mis'ar, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tawus, from Uthman ibn Affan, he said: The mu'li is stopped at the expiry of the four; he must either return or divorce."
"11340","From Malik and Ma'mar and Ibn Uyaynah, from Ayyub, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Marwan stopped a man who took an ila oath from his wife after six months."
"11341","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hisham ibn Yahya said to Ata: If a person is ignorant of the term of ila until four months pass. He said: Even if he is ignorant, the term of that is as Allah has ordained."
"11342","From al-Thawri, or one who narrates to me informed me, from Mansur and Mughirah and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, that a man called Abdullah ibn Anis took an ila oath from his wife, and four months passed before he had intercourse with her, then he had intercourse with her after the four while not remembering his oath. He came to Alqamah ibn Qays and mentioned that to him, then they came to Ibn Mas'ud and asked him. He said: She has become separated from you, so propose to her herself; so he proposed to her herself and gave her a ratl of silver as dower."
"11343","Abd al-Razzaq said: And I wrote to Umar ibn al-Mujalid, and he wrote to me that his father informed him, from Amir, he said: A man of Nakha who had been absent came and said to his companions: I left while angry with my wife, and I came while pleased, so I fell upon her, though I had sworn not to approach her, and the months had gone. His companions said to him: This is ila; go to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and ask him. He came to Abdullah and asked him. Abdullah said: Did you fall upon her? He said: Yes, and I did not know. Abdullah said: She has become separated from you with an irrevocable divorce; you have no return over her except if she wishes. Go inform her of that, then propose to her if she wishes. He came to her and informed her of the news, and she said: I return to my husband."
"11344","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, about a man who took an ila oath from his wife and did not have intercourse with her. He said: That is not ila, even if they remain more than four months, even if he is able to have intercourse with her."
"11345","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who married a woman, then her family opposed him, so he swore not to consummate with her for a year. He said: We do not consider this, and Allah knows best, like the mu'li; ila is only after entry. The imam only orders him to return by expiating his oath and hastening consummation with his family."
"11346","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: I asked Ibn al-Musayyib about: For those who take an ila oath from their wives. He said: It is nothing; they consider that to be before entry."
"11347","From Ibrahim ibn Umar, from Abu al-Jahm, that al-Hasan and Makhul used to reject ila before entry. From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, similar."
"11348","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from Yazid al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Fay' is intercourse."
"11349","From Ma'mar, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, that a man took an ila oath from his wife, then she gave birth before four months passed, and he wanted to return by fay' but could not because of the blood, until four months passed. He asked Alqamah ibn Qays and al-Aswad ibn Yazid about it, and they said: Have you not already taken her back in yourself? He said: Yes. They said: Then she is your wife."
"11350","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and Masruq, about a man who took an ila oath from his wife while she was pregnant, then she gave birth and he wanted to return but feared she would not become pure until four months passed; they ruled for him to return by tongue."
"11351","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: If he has an excuse of illness or old age or imprisonment, it suffices him to return by tongue. Ma'mar said: And I heard al-Zuhri saying similar to the saying of al-Hasan."
"11352","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Fay' is intercourse; there is no excuse for him except to have intercourse, even if he is in prison or on a journey. Sa'id is the speaker."
"11353","From al-Thawri, from Ali ibn Budhaymah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Fay' is intercourse."
"11354","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Fay' is intercourse; there is nothing below it except from an excuse or ignorance. Then he said afterwards: If he calls witnesses and enters upon her, it suffices him; he has returned. And his first saying is more pleasing to me."
"11355","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: If he returns in himself, it suffices him; she is his wife."
"11356","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Sha'tha, he said: That does not suffice him; it is nothing until he speaks with his tongue."
"11357","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a man who took an ila oath from his wife while she was pregnant, then she gave birth before four months passed and he did not return. He said: Let him complete four months; if he returns before the four, she is his wife. Ma'mar said: And I myself adopt the saying of Alqamah ibn Qays bearing upon that."
"11358","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I say: If he takes an ila oath from her and she gives birth before four months pass and he has not returned, let him complete four months. If they pass and she gives birth after them by a night or whatever, then she has become lawful. And if he dies leaving her while she is pregnant, though he had taken an ila oath from her and had not returned, her term is to lay her burden."
"11359","From al-Thawri, about a man who takes an ila oath from his wife then one of them dies while she is pregnant. He said: They inherit from one another so long as the four have not passed."
"11360","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, about a man who took an ila oath from his wife while she was pregnant, then died before four months passed while she was pregnant. They said: She inherits from him, and her term is to lay her burden."
"11361","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: If he divorces, then she menstruates one or two menstruations, then he takes her back, then takes an ila oath, she begins ila of four months from the day he takes the oath."
"11362","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If a man takes an ila oath from his wife, then two months pass, then he takes another oath and had not returned in that, let her begin four months from the latter ila. But if he returned, then took another oath, she begins the waiting period from the latter ila."
"11363","From al-Thawri, about a man who took an ila oath from his wife, then two months passed without approaching her, then he divorced her a second divorce, then took her back. He said: He begins ila anew of four months."
"11364","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: If a man takes an ila oath, then before the four pass he divorces and does not return, she begins the waiting period of a divorced woman from the day he divorced her. He said: That is when he resolved divorce, and ila at that point is nothing; she is his wife so long as her waiting period has not ended. And I myself say: If he divorces her, then a menstruation passes, then he takes her back, then takes an ila oath from her and does not have intercourse with her, she observes four months from the day he takes the oath, like divorce. And if he does not take her back until he takes the oath, she observes only for divorce, just as if he divorced her and did not take her back, she observes only for the first, for the divorce, because the waiting period of the first ended before the waiting period of the divorce, so it is one."
"11365","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: Divorce demolishes ila, and ila does not demolish divorce."
"11366","From Ma'mar, from one who heard al-Hasan saying: Neither of them demolishes the other."
"11367","From Ma'mar, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from al-Sha'bi, he said: If he takes an ila oath, then divorces, and the four months pass before the waiting period of divorce ends, they are two divorces. And if the waiting period of divorce ends before four months pass, it is one divorce."
"11368","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was told, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: If he takes an ila oath then divorces, the divorce nullifies the ila. And if he divorces then takes an ila oath, the ila stands."
"11369","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: If he divorces then takes an ila oath, or takes an ila oath then divorces, both occur together."
"11370","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: If a man divorces, then takes an ila oath, and takes an ila oath, then divorces, the divorce demolishes, and the ila is nothing, except that upon him, if he has intercourse after that, is an expiation."
"11371","Hammad said: And al-Sha'bi used to say: They are two racing horses. If the waiting period of divorce, three menstruations, passes before it passes, the ila is nothing, because the ila occurred while she was not his wife. And if the term of ila passes before the waiting period ends, both occur together. And the ila is nothing except that he marries her afterwards, then the ila remains as it is."
"11372","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was told that Ibn Mas'ud said: If he takes an ila oath then divorces, they are two racing horses. He said: And I say: If the waiting period of ila passes before the waiting period of divorce, it is one, because the waiting period of ila ended while she was his wife, so she observes the remainder of her waiting period from the divorce, just as if he divorced her and did not take her back, she observes only for her first divorce. And if the waiting period of divorce ends before the waiting period of ila, the ila is not a divorce; the ila occurred while she was not his wife."
"11373","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Ata about a man who takes an ila oath from his wife and does not have intercourse with her. He said: That is not ila, even if more than four months pass. He said: I said: Even if he is able to have intercourse with her? He said: Even so, even so; that is only when he is able to touch her."
"11374","From Ma'mar, Qatadah said: He expiates even if he had not entered with her."
"11375","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ila is only after entry, but he expiates for his oath."
"11376","From al-Thawri, about a man whom a woman passed by, and he took an ila oath not to approach her, then married her afterwards, then left her until four months passed. He said: It is not ila, but he expiates for his oath by feeding ten poor persons, because the ila occurred while she was not his wife. But if he said: If I marry her, by Allah I shall not approach her, then if he marries her, ila occurs."
"11377","From al-Nu'man ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu al-Jahm, from al-Hasan and Makhul, they said: Ila falls upon him even if he has not entered. Allah the Exalted said: For those who take an ila oath from their wives."
"11378","From al-Thawri, he said: If he takes an ila oath from four wives, if he falls upon some of them to the exclusion of others, there is no breach upon him in what he fell upon, and ila falls upon those who remain. When he falls upon them all together, the breach occurs at the last of them. And if he leaves them all, ila occurs."
"11379","From al-Thawri, about a man who had two wives and swore not to approach them, then fell upon one of them. He said: No expiation falls upon him, and ila is upon them both together. And if he swore not to have intercourse with either of them, then fell upon one of them, he has broken his oath, and upon the other there is neither ila nor expiation. And if he leaves them both until the term passes, he said: There is no expiation upon him for the one he fell upon, nor ila, and ila falls upon the remaining one. And if he does not fall upon either of them, ila falls upon them both together."
"11380","From al-Thawri, about a man who took an ila oath while ill, then recovered and remained the four months while healthy, then died after the four during the waiting period: they inherit from one another, for he is in the position of one who divorces while ill. And if he took an ila oath while healthy, then fell ill and remained ill until the four passed, then died during the waiting period, they do not inherit from one another."
"11381","From al-Thawri, about a man who took an ila oath from his wife, then four months passed, then he was asked and said: I had intercourse with her. He said: When the four pass and he claims he had intercourse with her during the four, he is not believed, then the saying is his saying."
"11382","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: They used to consider that when he returns, there is no expiation upon him. He said: And Ibrahim used to recommend expiation."
"11383","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: When he returns, there is no expiation upon him. And he says: But if they return, then Allah is Forgiving, Merciful."
"11384","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, they said: When a man divorces a woman once or twice, then dies leaving her before her waiting period ends, she observes the waiting period of one whose husband died, from the day he dies, and she inherits from him."
"11385","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If he divorces her while not pregnant, then dies leaving her, she begins the waiting period of one whose husband died, from the day he dies."
"11386","From al-Thawri, about a man who divorces his wife then dies leaving her while she is in her waiting period. He said: She observes four months and ten days if he owns the return, and she inherits from him."
"11387","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Ibn Abbas used to say: If he divorces her while pregnant, then dies leaving her, it is the latter of the two terms. Or he dies leaving her while she is pregnant, it is the latter of the two terms. It was said to him: And for those laden, their term is to lay their burden. He said: That is in divorce."
"11388","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If he divorces her pregnant, when she lays as soon as she lays, let her marry if she wishes, while she is in her blood, not yet pure."
"11389","From Ma'mar and al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, he said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Whomsoever wishes, I shall invoke mutual curse with him that this verse in the short Surah of Women: And for those laden, their term is to lay their burden, was revealed after the verse in al-Baqarah: And those who die among you and leave wives, they shall wait by themselves. He said: And it reached him that Ali said: It is the latter of the two terms, so he said that."
"11390","From Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Atiyyah, he said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud saying: The verse of the short Women: And for those laden, their term is to lay their burden, was revealed after the one in al-Baqarah: And those who die among you and leave wives, they shall wait by themselves."
"11391","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim informed me that Ibn Mas'ud said: The short Surah of Women: O Prophet, when you divorce women, was revealed after the long one in al-Baqarah."
"11392","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq informed me that a woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said to him: I gave birth after the death of my husband before the waiting period ended. Umar said: You are for the latter of the two terms. She passed by Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and he said to her: Where did you come from? She mentioned to him and informed him of what Umar said. He said: Go to Umar and say to him: Ubayy ibn Ka'b says: You have become lawful, and if you seek me, I am here. She went to Umar and informed him. He said: Call him. She came to him and found him praying, and he did not hasten from his prayer until he finished it, then he went with her to him. Umar said to him: What does this woman say? Ubayy said: I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And for those laden, their term is to lay their burden, then the pregnant woman whose husband died, that she lay her burden. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Yes. Umar said to the woman: Listen to what you hear."
"11393","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: When she lays her burden, her term has become lawful. He said: And he said: A man of the Ansar said: I heard your father saying: If she laid her burden while he was upon his bed, not yet buried, she would become lawful."
"11394","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When she lays her burden, her term has become lawful. He said: A man of the Ansar told him that Umar said: If she laid her burden while he was upon his bed, not yet buried, she would become lawful for husbands."
"11395","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: She may marry if she wishes while in her blood. And another than him said: The hour she lays."
"11396","From al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from al-Zubayr, that under him was Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah, and she said: Set my mind at ease, so he divorced her once, then she laid her burden, and he came and said: She deceived me; may Allah deceive her. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: The decree has preceded; propose to her herself."
"11397","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, he said: Marwan sent Abdullah ibn Utbah to Subay'ah bint al-Harith, asking her about what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ruled for her. She informed him that she was under Sa'd ibn Khawlah, and he died leaving her in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he was a Badri. She laid her burden before four months and ten days from his death passed for her. Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak met her when she had risen from her bleeding, having applied kohl, and said: Perhaps you desire marriage; it is four months and ten days from the death of your husband. He said: She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned to him what Abu al-Sanabil said. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: You have become lawful when you laid your burden."
"11398","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayrah were asked about a man who died leaving his wife, and she gave birth before four months passed for her. Ibn Abbas said: She observes the latter of the two terms. Abu Salamah said: I said: When she lays her burden, her term has become lawful? Abu Hurayrah said: I am with the son of my brother, meaning Abu Salamah. Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayrah sent to Umm Salamah, while she was in her chamber and they were in the mosque, asking her about that. She informed that Subay'ah bint al-Harith, her husband died leaving her, and she gave birth nights after his death. Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak met her when she had risen from her bleeding, having applied kohl and worn garments, and said: Perhaps you see that you have become lawful; you do not become lawful until four months and ten days from the death of your husband pass for you. When evening came, she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned to him her affair and what Abu al-Sanabil said to her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: When you lay your burden, your term has become lawful. He said: And I thought that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Abu al-Sanabil has lied. From Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayrah and Abu Salamah sent to Umm Salamah Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas."
"11399","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Asim informed me that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, he said: While I and Abu Hurayrah were with Ibn Abbas, a woman came to him and said: My husband died leaving me while I was pregnant. She mentioned that she gave birth in less than four months from the day he died leaving her. Ibn Abbas said: You are for the latter of the two terms. Abu Salamah said: I said: I have knowledge. Ibn Abbas said: Bring the woman. Abu Salamah said: A man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Her husband died leaving her and she gave birth. She informed him of less than four months from the day he died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Subay'ah, restrain yourself. Abu Hurayrah said: And I bear witness to that. Ibn Abbas said to the woman: Listen to what you hear."
"11400","From Malik, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Umm Salamah informed him that Subay'ah gave birth after the death of her husband by half a month."
"11401","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that he informed him, or he heard him saying: Subay'ah gave birth seven nights from the day her husband died leaving her."
"11402","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Subay'ah gave birth seven nights from the day her husband died leaving her."
"11403","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Muslim informed me that Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, told them that Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth after the death of her husband by forty-five. Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered her to marry. Ibn Jurayj said: And one whom I trust told me that Subay'ah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after she gave birth by fifteen."
"11404","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man dies leaving his wife pregnant, her term is to lay her burden. And he mentioned that Subay'ah gave birth after the death of her husband by twenty, or he said: seventeen nights, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to marry."
"11405","From Ma'mar, some of them say: She remained seventeen nights, and among them who says: forty nights."
"11406","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Isma'il ibn Muhammad and Ya'qub ibn Utbah and others than them said, from Umm Salamah, she said: Subay'ah gave birth and bore after the death of her husband by half a month."
"11407","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah said: Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah, her husband died leaving her while she was pregnant, and she did not remain but nights until she gave birth. When she became free of bleeding, she was proposed to. She sought permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for marriage when she gave birth, and he permitted her, so she married."
"11408","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: If she laid her burden while he was upon his bed, not yet buried, she would become lawful."
"11409","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: I said: Even if it is a morsel or a clot? He said: Yes. Ma'mar said: And Qatadah said similar to the saying of al-Zuhri. And al-Zuhri said: When a woman miscarries a distinct miscarriage, her term has become lawful. And when a slave woman miscarries a distinct miscarriage, it is not lawful for him to sell her."
"11410","From Ma'mar, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, that Ali ibn Abi Talib said: About a man who marries a woman then dies leaving her, without entering with her and without fixing for her: he used to assign for her the inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period, and assign for her no dower."
"11411","From al-Thawri, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abd Khayr, from Ali: That he used to assign for her the inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period, and assign for her no dower."
"11412","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi ibn Umar, and from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he married off his son Waqid, then he died before entering, without fixing anything for her. Ibn Umar assigned for her no dower. Her mother refused but to dispute him. Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab came to him and said: Her mother refuses but to dispute you, and the saying is as you say. Ibn Umar said: I do not like that you leave a right if it is yours. He disputed him to Zayd ibn Thabit. Zayd assigned for her no dower, and assigned for her the inheritance."
"11413","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying about a man who marries a woman, without touching her and without fixing a dower for her, until he dies. He said: The inheritance suffices her, and there is no dower for her. If he had fixed a dower for her, then for her is a dower, and for her is the inheritance."
"11414","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: There is no dower for her; the inheritance suffices her."
"11415","Ma'mar informed us, he said: Ibn Tawus informed us, from his father, that he used to say: There is no dower for her when he dies, without fixing for her and without entering with her, until he heard of the hadith of Ibn Mas'ud, then he refrained from it, and did not say anything about it."
"11416","Ma'mar informed us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, and from Qatadah also, that a man came to Ibn Mas'ud and asked him about a woman whose husband died leaving her, without entering with her and without fixing for her. Ibn Mas'ud said to him: Ask the people, for the people are many, or as he said. The man said: By Allah, if I remained a year, I would not ask other than you. He said: Ibn Mas'ud put him off for a month, then stood and performed ablution, then bowed two rak'ahs, then said: O Allah, whatever is correct is from You, and whatever is error is from me. Then he said: I consider for her the dower of one of her women, without diminution and without excess, and for her is the inheritance with that, and upon her is the waiting period. A man of Ashja' stood and said: I bear witness that you have judged in it by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Barwa' bint Washiq, who was under Hilal ibn Umayyah. Ibn Mas'ud said: Did anyone hear this with you? He said: Yes. He brought a group of his people, and they bore witness to that. He said: They did not see Ibn Mas'ud rejoice at anything as he rejoiced at that, when it agreed with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11417","He said: Ma'mar informed us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from al-Hakam, he said: That reached Ali, and he said: The Bedouins are not to be believed about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11418","From al-Thawri, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud was approached and asked about a man who married a woman, without fixing for her and without touching her until he died. He said: He put them off, then said: I shall say in it by my opinion; if it is correct, it is from Allah, and if it is error, it is from me. I consider for her the dower of a woman of her women, without diminution and without excess, and upon her is the waiting period, and for her is the inheritance. Ma'qil ibn Sinan al-Ashja'i stood and said: I bear witness that you have judged in it by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Barwa' bint Washiq, a woman of Banu Ru'as, and Banu Ru'as is a clan of Banu Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah. From Ma'mar: Al-Hasan and Qatadah were in it upon the saying of Ibn Mas'ud."
"11419","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: Every divorce whose marriage was sound, when they separate in that marriage, even if he does not speak divorce, it is one: mubara'ah and fidyah. Except that Ibn Abbas did not use to say that."
"11420","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: Every separation in a marriage that was upon the face of marriage is one divorce, like the form of fidyah, and the slave woman freed, and she who chooses herself, and she whose husband is lost then her husband comes and he chooses his wife, then the other returns her, and she who is under a Christian then he becomes Muslim, then he marries her after that. He says: It is one in the likes of this."
"11421","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman made fidyah one divorce. If divorce is followed when she ransoms from him in that sitting, it binds her."
"11422","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Zuhri, he said: Fidyah is one divorce."
"11423","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Abi Najih, he said: Khul' is one divorce."
"11424","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Khul' is one irrevocable divorce. And khul' is what is below the headband of the head. And a woman may ransom with some of her wealth."
"11425","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Mas'ud used not to consider a divorce irrevocable except in khul' or ila."
"11426","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, and from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and Ibn al-Musayyib, they said: When a man accepts the wealth, even if he does not divorce, it is one."
"11427","From Hushaym, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Husayn al-Harithi, from al-Sha'bi, that Ali said: When he takes a price for divorce, it is one."
"11428","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When a man buys divorce from his wife, it is khul'. And Qatadah said: It is not khul'."
"11429","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Asim, that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed him that a woman was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, and he had dowered her a garden, and he was jealous, so he struck her and broke her hand. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained to him. She said: I return to him his garden. He said: Will you do so? She said: Yes. He called her husband and said: She returns to you your garden. He said: Is that for me? He said: Yes. He said: I have accepted, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go, it is one. Then she married after him Rifa'ah al-Abidi, and he struck her. She came to Uthman and said: I return to him his dower. Uthman called him, and he accepted. Uthman said: Go, it is one. Ibn Jurayj said: And he informed me from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, similar to the report of Dawud, except that he said: He wounded her. From al-Muthanna, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, similar."
"11430","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, he said: The wife of Thabit ibn Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I do not blame Thabit for religion nor character, but I dislike disbelief in Islam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you return to him his garden? She said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Thabit, took his garden, and separated him. She is Jamilah bint Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul. Ma'mar said: And it reached me that she said that day: I dislike to disobey my Lord. He said: And it reached me that she said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have of beauty what you see, and Thabit is an ugly man."
"11431","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Jumhan, that Umm Bakr al-Aslamiyyah was under Abdullah ibn Asid, then she sought khul' from him. Then she regretted and he regretted. He came to Uthman and informed him. He said: It is one divorce, unless you named something, then it is upon what you named. So he took her back."
"11432","From Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, that Uthman made fidyah divorce. He said: If he intends anything of divorce, it is with the fidyah."
"11433","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me that Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman told him that Habibah bint Sahl told her that Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas reached of beating her, he does not know what it is. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the darkness before dawn, and mentioned to him what was with her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take from her. She said: Indeed what he gave me is with me as it is. He said: Take from her. He took from her. Amrah said: She sat with her family."
"11434","From Ma'mar, from Thawr, from Maymun ibn Mihran, he said in the reading of Ubayy: Fidyah is one divorce. Ma'mar said: I mentioned that to Ayyub, then we came to a man with whom was an old mushaf of Ubayy, come from a trustworthy source, and we read in it: Except that they think they will not uphold the bounds of Allah, there is no blame upon them in what she ransoms with; she is not lawful to him after until she marries another husband."
"11435","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I saw a woman disputing her husband to Shurayh, and she said to him: Divorce me, and to you is what is upon you. He divorced her. She said: No, by Allah, until you pass them. He did. The companions of Shurayh said: Your wife has gone from you, and we do not see your wealth but gone. Shurayh said: If Islam were as you say, it would be narrower than the edge of a sword."
"11436","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: He informed me that Hasan ibn Muslim, that Tawus said: I was with Ibn Abbas when Ibrahim ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas asked him and said: I am employed here, and Ibn al-Zubayr employed him over Yemen over alms-taxes, so teach me divorce, for most of their divorce is fidyah. Ibn Abbas said: It is not one. And he used to allow it, separating by it. He said: And he used to say: It is only fidyah, but the people have mistaken its name. Hasan ibn Muslim said to me: Tawus said: I returned to Ibn Abbas after that, and he said: Fidyah is not divorce. He said: And I used to hear Ibn Abbas reciting about that: And divorced women shall wait by themselves three courses. Then he says: Then there is no blame upon them in what she ransoms with. Then he mentioned divorce after fidyah. He said: And he used to say: Allah mentioned divorce before fidyah and after it, and Allah mentioned fidyah between that, and I do not hear Him mention in fidyah divorce. He said: And he did not consider it a divorce."
"11437","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus said to me: My father did not consider fidyah divorce, and he allowed it between them."
"11438","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Tawus, that he said: Were it not that it is knowledge, it is not lawful for me to conceal it, meaning fidyah, I would not have told it to anyone. He said: Ibn Abbas did not consider fidyah divorce until he divorces. Then he says: Do you not see that He mentioned divorce before it, then mentioned fidyah, and did not make it divorce, then said in the second: Then if he divorces her, she is not lawful to him after until she marries another husband. And He did not make fidyah between them divorce."
"11439","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, saying: Whatever wealth allows is not divorce. He said: And I do not think he informed me it except from Ibn Abbas. I said to Amr: She said: If you divorce me three times, your wealth is returned to you, and that is not until you speak divorce three times. He did. He said: One, then he entered it in it. And Ikrimah said: He said: And I say: Everything he takes from her is fidyah."
"11440","From Ma'mar, from Hammad, he said: Every separation that was from the husband is one divorce, and every separation from the wife is nothing."
"11441","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, I think, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Everything wealth allows is not divorce, meaning khul'."
"11442","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd asked Ibn Abbas about a man who divorced his wife two divorces, then she sought khul' from him, may he marry her? He said: Yes. Allah mentioned divorce in the first of the verse and its end, and khul' between that, so there is no harm in it."
"11443","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Ata about a man who divorced after fidyah. He said: Nothing is counted, because he divorced a woman over whom he owns nothing. Sulayman ibn Musa rejected it, and Ata said: Ibn Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr agreed on that, about a man who took khul' from his wife then divorced her after the khul'. They agreed that he divorced after the khul', so nothing is counted. They said: He did not divorce his wife; he only divorced what he does not own."
"11444","From Ibn Jurayj, and Ibn Tawus claimed, from his father, that he used to say: If he divorces her after fidyah during the waiting period, it is allowed."
"11445","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, and from Matar, from al-Hasan, they said: About the woman who ransoms, if he divorces her when he ransoms with her, and follows it in that sitting, divorce binds her. And if he divorces her after they separate, it does not bind her."
"11446","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah Abd al-Rahman, he said: If she is divorced during the waiting period after fidyah, it is nothing."
"11447","From Ma'mar, from Hafs ibn Abi Sulayman, that al-Hasan said: His divorce during the waiting period after khul' is nothing. Qatadah said: Al-Hasan had once said other than that."
"11448","From Abu Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ikrimah saying: Divorce after fidyah is nothing."
"11449","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: If he divorces her after fidyah during the waiting period, it is allowed, so his divorce is allowed."
"11450","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: If he divorces after fidyah during the waiting period, his divorce is allowed."
"11451","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyib and al-Nakha'i, they said: His divorce during the waiting period is allowed."
"11452","From al-Thawri, from Bayan, from al-Sha'bi, and Mansur and al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, about the divorce of the woman who ransoms during the waiting period? They said: Whatever divorce follows her during the waiting period binds her."
"11453","From Isma'il ibn Ayyash, he said: Al-Ala ibn Utbah al-Yahsibi informed me, from Ali ibn Talhah al-Hashimi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman who seeks khul' is in divorce so long as she is in the waiting period. We mentioned it to al-Thawri, and he said: We asked about it and found for it no origin."
"11454","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Abd al-Karim, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, he said: If a woman observes waiting while the fluid of the man is in her womb, she observes waiting from him, and does not observe waiting from other than him. He may marry her, and other than him may not marry her. And divorce falls upon her during the waiting period."
"11455","From Ma'mar, from Umar ibn Rashid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: Divorce runs upon the woman who seeks khul', so long as she is in the waiting period. I told it to Ma'mar, and he said: I heard Yahya mentioning it, from Ibn Mas'ud."
"11456","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If she ransoms herself from him (by khul') and then he divorces her during the waiting period, it does not take effect on her. If he marries her during her waiting period, then divorces her before consummating with her and without having touched her, while he had fixed a dower for her, then she observes the rest of her waiting period, and she is entitled to half her dower."
"11457","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: If he divorces her during the waiting period, the divorce does not take effect on her. If he marries her, then divorces her before consummating with her, she gets half the dower, she has more right to herself, and the waiting period continues from the first waiting period."
"11458","From Ma'mar — and I asked him about a man whose wife ransoms herself from him, then he marries her during her waiting period, then divorces her before consummating with her: she gets half the dower, and she has more right to herself. He said: Al-Hasan, Qatadah and al-Zuhri used to say: She gets half the dower, and she completes the remainder of the waiting period."
"11459","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, concerning a man who marries a woman, then swears an oath of abstention (ila') from her, and four months pass without his taking her back, then he proposes to her and marries her, then divorces her before consummating with her, he said: She gets half the dower and completes the remainder of the waiting period; if she has not menstruated, she starts the waiting period anew. Ma'mar said: Al-Hasan said the same. He said: And it reached me that al-Nakha'i used to say: The full dower is due to her."
"11460","From al-Thawri, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Fudayl, from Ibrahim — and al-Hasan also mentioned it from al-Sha'bi — he said: When one marries a woman separated by khul', or one against whom ila' was sworn, and every irrevocable divorce, if he marries her during the waiting period and divorces her once before consummating with her, she gets the full dower and she remains his wife. Both say: She does not separate from him, and she begins a new waiting period for this divorce from the day he divorced her, while the first waiting period is nullified by his marrying her. If he divorces her twice, she is separated from him with three divorces counting the khul', she gets the full dower, and she begins a new waiting period. Sufyan holds this view. He said: And in their view, he may marry her only with a proposal."
"11461","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who swore an oath involving divorce of his wife, then did what he had sworn about during the waiting period, he said: It takes effect against him in the view of Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi; it does not take effect against him in the view of Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan."
"11462","From Ata, concerning a man who had divorced his wife three times, in a case of a creditor where she had ransomed herself from him before he incurred sin, then he incurred sin within the term before his creditor settled that, then he wished to marry her, so he came to Ata and mentioned that to him, and he said: Marry her."
"11463","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If he wishes to marry her during her waiting period, it is with a new dower and a new proposal."
"11464","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: They do not inherit from one another during the waiting period, and he has no right to take her back unless she wills. If she does so, it is with a proposal and a dower."
"11465","From Ma'mar, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, they both said: If her husband wishes, and she wishes, he may marry her during her waiting period, as long as he has not made her divorce final, with a new dower."
"11466","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: He may take her back only with a proposal. Qatadah said: And that may only be in the presence of a guardian."
"11467","From Ma'mar, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, they both said: If one of them dies during the waiting period, they do not inherit from one another."
"11468","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: If he wishes to take her back, let him return to her what he took from her during the waiting period, and let him call witnesses to her return. Ma'mar said: Al-Zuhri used to say the same."
"11469","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah and al-Hasan, they both said: When a man says to his wife, 'If you forgo what I owe you, you are divorced,' then they are two divorces. Al-Zuhri used to say: The ransom is one divorce; if he adds anything, it goes along with the ransom."
"11470","From Ma'mar, from one of the scholars, he said: When a man says, 'If you forgo such-and-such for me, you are divorced,' and she forgoes it, then it is one divorce."
"11471","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who said to his wife, 'If you forgo what is due upon me, you are divorced,' he said: It is khul', one irrevocable divorce."
"11472","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Shurayh, concerning a woman who said to her husband, 'I will buy one divorce from you for one hundred dirhams,' and he did so, he said: I do not consider it a ransom; it is one divorce, and he has more right to her."
"11473","From Ma'mar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about it, and he said: I consider it khul'."
"11474","From al-Thawri, from Hammad — and our companions said — concerning a man whose wife said to him, 'I will buy one divorce from you for a dinar,' he said: It is khul', and if he stipulates return, it is nothing; his stipulation is nothing."
"11475","From al-Thawri, concerning a man whose wife owed him a thousand dirhams, and she said, 'Divorce me once, and I will grant you two years' respite for the thousand,' so he divorced her once, then she delayed payment from him, he said: He retains the right of return over her; this is not a ransom, because he took nothing."
"11476","From al-Thawri, he said: And I asked him about a woman who said, 'If you place my affair in my hand, you shall have all my dower owed by you,' and he said, 'Your affair is in your hand,' and she said, 'Then I am divorced three times,' he said: It is one irrevocable divorce."
"11477","From al-Thawri, concerning a man whose wife said to him, 'Sell me three divorces for a thousand dirhams,' and he divorced her once, then refused, he said to him: Three thousand, and it is one irrevocable divorce. If she said to him, 'I will give you a thousand dirhams if you divorce me three times,' then if he divorces her three times he gets the thousand dirhams, but if he divorces her once or twice he gets nothing, and he has more right to her."
"11478","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata, a man said to his wife, 'If you give me what is mine, you are divorced,' and she did so, he said: It is one divorce, the divorce of ransom. Amr said the same."
"11479","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata, she said, 'I will give you your property, and my affair shall be in my hand,' and he said, 'Your affair is in your hand' — does she divorce herself? He said: No, it is only a ransom, not a transfer of authority."
"11480","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: If he takes even one dirham from her on condition that her affair is in her hand, then it is only the ransom. I said: She may not divorce herself? He said: No."
"11481","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Shihab al-Khawlani, that a woman who had ransomed herself from her husband with a thousand dirhams was brought before Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he upheld it."
"11482","From Ma'mar, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi', she said: I ransomed myself from my husband, then I regretted it, and that was raised to Uthman, and he upheld it."
"11483","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi', that al-Rubayyi' ransomed herself from her husband, and Ibn Umar raised that to Uthman, and he upheld it."
"11484","From Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, that he used to uphold khul' without the ruler."
"11485","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: Khul' may only take place before the ruler."
"11486","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: It is not lawful for a man to take anything from his wife as ransom until the recalcitrance comes from her side. It was said to him: How does recalcitrance occur? He said: Recalcitrance is that she shows him hatred, treats him badly in companionship, shows him dislike, and disobeys his command."
"11487","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Abu al-Sha'tha, he said: When the recalcitrance comes from her side, her ransom is lawful for him."
"11488","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: It is not lawful for him to take more than what he gave her, and he does not agree with those who say: It is not lawful for him to take a ransom from her until she says, 'I will not uphold the bounds of Allah, nor bathe from major impurity.'"
"11489","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: He holds to what Allah said, 'Except that they both fear they will not uphold the bounds of Allah.' He said: He did not hold the view of the foolish, that it is not lawful for him until she says, 'I will not bathe for you from major impurity,' but he says: Except that they both fear they will not uphold the bounds of Allah concerning what is enjoined upon each of them toward the other in companionship and company."
"11490","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If she calls him to it in anger or otherwise, and he acts, while she was obedient to him, then she should return to him; she has nothing unless it is the third divorce, and then she is gone."
"11491","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata — I said to him: What if she was disobedient to him and offensive between him and her, and he calls her to khul', is it lawful? He said: No; either he is content and keeps her, or he releases her; and he himself has no right to treat her badly so that she ransoms herself."
"11492","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: If he was good to her, and she was obedient to him with good companionship, then she called him in anger to her ransom and he acted, I do not think he may take her property."
"11493","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr said, unless he treats her badly, constraining her, then it is not permitted; even if she calls him to it. And I say: As for what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted of ransom."
"11494","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, he said: Abu Qilabah used to hold that when a woman commits adultery and her husband discovers it, he may beat her until she ransoms herself from him."
"11495","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muzani, from Ali ibn Wahb, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: Three things make a woman's khul' lawful: if she corrupts your property against you, or you call her to find comfort with her and she refuses you, or she goes out without your permission."
